1
00:00:11,740 --> 00:00:12,570
Yes...

2
00:00:13,860 --> 00:00:17,700
I've always felt as though there is someone beyond the window.

3
00:00:21,620 --> 00:00:27,170
But, there's not the slightest chance of anyone being there.

4
00:00:31,920 --> 00:00:33,930
I wake up, and I regret.

5
00:00:34,550 --> 00:00:36,800
I regret looking for that someone.

6
00:00:37,550 --> 00:00:39,680
Just like always.

7
00:00:45,520 --> 00:00:47,190
Dear Tomoya.

8
00:00:47,190 --> 00:00:51,440
It's your week's allowance and lunch money.

9
00:00:57,870 --> 00:01:01,160
Ah, right. It's time you go to school, isn't it?

10
00:01:01,160 --> 00:01:03,710
I just got back... from work.

11
00:01:04,750 --> 00:01:07,080
Did you pick up the money I left you?

12
00:01:13,590 --> 00:01:14,920
There is nowhere...

13
00:01:16,630 --> 00:01:18,090
...where I belong.

14
00:01:23,890 --> 00:01:28,520
But for no real reason... I did go to school.

15
00:01:33,780 --> 00:01:35,900
One of those force of habit things.

16
00:01:36,110 --> 00:01:48,420
Suki tooru yume o mite ita Yawarakai eien

17
00:01:36,110 --> 00:01:48,420
I was having a transparent dream
It was a tender eternity

18
00:01:42,910 --> 00:01:45,290
It's really beautiful.

19
00:01:45,290 --> 00:01:46,870
My heart is dancing.

20
00:01:49,420 --> 00:01:55,130
Kaze no yona kasuko na koe ga

21
00:01:49,420 --> 00:01:55,130
The faint, wind-like voice

22
00:01:51,040 --> 00:01:52,550
It's only now.

23
00:01:53,340 --> 00:01:55,420
In less then a week,

24
00:01:55,970 --> 00:02:02,010
Takai sora kara boku ho yonde iru

25
00:01:55,970 --> 00:02:02,010
Is calling me from the high sky
If I take off while like this

26
00:01:56,220 --> 00:01:58,050
they'll all fall to the ground.

27
00:02:01,970 --> 00:02:03,560
Yes, but...

28
00:02:02,600 --> 00:02:15,440
Kono mama tobi tateba doko ni datte yukeru

29
00:02:02,600 --> 00:02:15,440
I can go anywhere

30
00:02:03,560 --> 00:02:06,390
...they'll bloom again next year.

31
00:02:07,560 --> 00:02:13,190
They will bloom beautifully the year after that, and the year after that, too.

32
00:02:15,820 --> 00:02:22,240
Kasaneta teto te no nakani

33
00:02:15,820 --> 00:02:22,240
If we can see a little future

34
00:02:22,410 --> 00:02:28,920
Chiisana mirai ga mietara

35
00:02:22,410 --> 00:02:28,920
Within our joined hands

36
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:41,890
Hikari no naka yurameita kotobamo omoi mo zenbu

37
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:41,890
Then the words, thoughts, everything
That swayed in the light-

38
00:02:29,460 --> 00:02:30,420
We're late.

39
00:02:31,500 --> 00:02:34,210
The bell rang a long time ago.

40
00:02:38,220 --> 00:02:39,260
See ya.

41
00:02:41,970 --> 00:02:59,360
Harukana kimi made nokosazu tsutaete kitto

42
00:02:41,970 --> 00:02:59,360
Surely, I'll unreservedly tell them
To the distant you

43
00:02:42,430 --> 00:02:44,760
Um, if you don't mind...

44
00:02:45,140 --> 00:02:48,520
...will you walk up this hill together?

45
00:02:51,560 --> 00:02:53,190
Walk up the hill together?

46
00:02:54,270 --> 00:02:54,940
Why?

47
00:02:55,480 --> 00:02:58,070
I can make it this far every day.

48
00:02:58,490 --> 00:03:03,160
But no matter what, I can't walk up the rest of the hill.

49
00:03:03,870 --> 00:03:07,250
It's strange, isn't it? But I can't help it.

50
00:03:09,500 --> 00:03:13,170
Then... Then can I follow you?

51
00:03:13,460 --> 00:03:17,880
I'll just follow your back up the hill.

52
00:03:17,880 --> 00:03:19,630
Is that fine?

53
00:03:23,680 --> 00:03:25,640
I didn't answer her.

54
00:03:26,310 --> 00:03:30,270
It doesn't matter who walks behind me.

55
00:03:31,140 --> 00:03:34,730
I just walk wherever I want.

56
00:03:38,440 --> 00:03:39,190
But...

57
00:03:40,570 --> 00:03:42,160
But... Now that I think back...

58
00:03:42,660 --> 00:03:47,580
That was when I first met her.

59
00:03:48,950 --> 00:03:51,910
It was when everything began.

60
00:03:55,880 --> 00:03:58,750
I'm Furukawa Nagisa.

61
00:03:58,750 --> 00:03:59,840
What's your name?

62
00:04:00,300 --> 00:04:04,300
Why does it matter? You just followed me.

63
00:04:04,300 --> 00:04:09,770
I would want to know your name in case I see you next time and want to say hi.

64
00:04:10,350 --> 00:04:11,680
We won't see each other.

65
00:04:11,930 --> 00:04:13,900
Even if we do, just act like you don't know me.

66
00:04:14,270 --> 00:04:16,770
I'm Furukawa Nagisa.

67
00:04:17,020 --> 00:04:18,570
I heard that already.

68
00:04:19,610 --> 00:04:20,940
Yes.

69
00:04:22,740 --> 00:04:24,280
I'm Okazaki Tomoya.

70
00:04:24,490 --> 00:04:26,740
Okazaki Tomoya-san...

71
00:04:28,910 --> 00:04:30,660
Thank you very much.

72
00:04:30,870 --> 00:04:36,040
I was able to walk up the hill
and make it all the way to school.

73
00:04:41,210 --> 00:04:46,340
Hey, Okazaki, if you're that bored,
wake up Sunohara sitting next to you.

74
00:04:47,890 --> 00:04:50,350
Just so you know, he's not the best at waking up.

75
00:04:50,350 --> 00:04:52,310
I told you to wake him up, so wake him up!

76
00:04:53,430 --> 00:04:55,270
Hey, Sunohara, wake up.

77
00:05:05,530 --> 00:05:06,030
Sunohara!

78
00:05:06,490 --> 00:05:07,530
Don't bite my ear!

79
00:05:07,780 --> 00:05:10,080
Stop... Stop licking...

80
00:05:16,000 --> 00:05:18,580
Okazaki, what are you going to have for lunch?

81
00:05:19,170 --> 00:05:19,960
Bread.

82
00:05:20,880 --> 00:05:22,050
Bread, eh?

83
00:05:22,630 --> 00:05:26,840
Yeah, the cafeteria's stuffed bread is pretty good.

84
00:05:26,840 --> 00:05:27,930
But it's really crowded.

85
00:05:27,930 --> 00:05:28,800
Fried noodle bread!

86
00:05:28,800 --> 00:05:29,970
Ham cutlet bread!

87
00:05:29,970 --> 00:05:30,720
Ginger roast bread!

88
00:05:30,720 --> 00:05:33,310
So all the stuffed bread will be sold out.

89
00:05:34,230 --> 00:05:37,060
I'll pay for you, so go buy some.

90
00:05:37,480 --> 00:05:38,600
Seriously?

91
00:05:38,900 --> 00:05:40,650
In that case...

92
00:05:40,650 --> 00:05:42,360
I'll get myself moving!

93
00:05:43,990 --> 00:05:46,070
You wanna die or what?

94
00:05:46,070 --> 00:05:47,990
We're all in line, you see?

95
00:05:51,160 --> 00:05:52,120
Damn it...

96
00:05:53,830 --> 00:05:55,660
Never give up!

97
00:05:55,960 --> 00:05:59,460
Sunohara Youhei, swimming all the way to the goal.

98
00:05:59,630 --> 00:06:01,540
The gold medal he always dreamed of.

99
00:06:01,540 --> 00:06:02,840
The prize is stuffed bread.

100
00:06:02,840 --> 00:06:04,130
Go for it, Sunohara!

101
00:06:04,130 --> 00:06:05,420
Sunohara, you can do it!

102
00:06:08,880 --> 00:06:11,430
I told you not to cut.

103
00:06:28,240 --> 00:06:29,660
Okazaki-san.

104
00:06:30,490 --> 00:06:32,530
Okazaki Tomoya-san.

105
00:06:33,530 --> 00:06:35,240
This is a nice place, don't you think?

106
00:06:35,540 --> 00:06:39,170
The wind is nice, too, and it's quiet.

107
00:06:39,670 --> 00:06:41,330
Yeah, since it's off limits.

108
00:06:42,460 --> 00:06:45,130
When the lifestyle guidance staff finds you, you'll get yelled at.

109
00:06:45,760 --> 00:06:49,380
I'll say I'm sorry when that happens.

110
00:06:54,310 --> 00:06:55,810
Do you come here often?

111
00:06:56,140 --> 00:06:57,810
Um...

112
00:06:57,810 --> 00:06:58,770
Only from time to time?

113
00:06:59,690 --> 00:07:01,560
Today's the first time.

114
00:07:01,560 --> 00:07:07,030
It was my first time at school in a while, so I was wondering what I should do during the lunch break.

115
00:07:07,860 --> 00:07:11,320
Usually you spend it eating lunch.

116
00:07:11,320 --> 00:07:12,910
Unless, you've already eaten.

117
00:07:13,410 --> 00:07:14,580
Sweet bean bread.

118
00:07:14,870 --> 00:07:17,240
I'm about to buy sweet bean bread and eat.

119
00:07:17,580 --> 00:07:21,040
The sweet bean bread at the cafeteria is really good.

120
00:07:21,420 --> 00:07:23,710
It's crowded down there now because of the stuffed breads,

121
00:07:23,710 --> 00:07:27,250
but the sweet bean bread usually has leftovers, even though they're really good.

122
00:07:27,250 --> 00:07:29,760
So I go, buy them, and eat them.

123
00:07:38,970 --> 00:07:40,390
Okazaki!

124
00:07:40,980 --> 00:07:42,140
I made you wait...

125
00:07:42,140 --> 00:07:43,060
Sorry...

126
00:07:43,060 --> 00:07:44,190
I apologize...

127
00:07:45,310 --> 00:07:47,190
The food stand was crowded like crazy.

128
00:07:47,190 --> 00:07:51,360
Even with my best efforts,
I could only buy sweet bean bread.

129
00:07:51,950 --> 00:07:55,410
And that pissed me off, so I used the entire Â¥1000.

130
00:07:55,410 --> 00:07:57,830
You know I don't eat sweet bean bread.

131
00:07:58,200 --> 00:08:00,750
But given the situation, please, eat it.

132
00:08:10,260 --> 00:08:11,420
It's yours.

133
00:08:11,420 --> 00:08:12,300
Sweet bean bread.

134
00:08:13,010 --> 00:08:14,640
You haven't had lunch yet, right?

135
00:08:15,680 --> 00:08:16,550
Bye.

136
00:08:17,560 --> 00:08:19,060
Hey, Okazaki!

137
00:08:19,060 --> 00:08:20,980
I said wait! Tomoya!

138
00:08:38,160 --> 00:08:40,080
Right. The Founders Festival's coming up.

139
00:08:40,290 --> 00:08:42,710
All the clubs are working hard with preparations.

140
00:08:44,040 --> 00:08:47,380
Compared to that, we aren't in any clubs, so we have it easy.

141
00:08:50,670 --> 00:08:54,760
So Okazaki, who was that girl on the roof?

142
00:08:55,130 --> 00:08:56,090
I don't know.

143
00:08:57,180 --> 00:08:58,550
You're going to play dumb?

144
00:08:59,140 --> 00:09:01,220
She's Furukawa Nagisa.

145
00:09:01,220 --> 00:09:02,640
I don't know anything more than that.

146
00:09:02,640 --> 00:09:05,350
That's enough to say you know her.

147
00:09:08,270 --> 00:09:12,530
But I don't recall seeing her on campus before.

148
00:09:14,200 --> 00:09:20,660
It's intolerable how students are oblivious to the problems this school is facing.

149
00:09:21,120 --> 00:09:26,330
The student council must be clear on these problems and state them to the school!

150
00:09:26,790 --> 00:09:30,800
That is the reason why I am announcing my bid for student council president!

151
00:09:31,090 --> 00:09:33,630
Sakagami Tomoyo! Sakagami Tomoyo!

152
00:09:33,880 --> 00:09:38,800
I strongly believe that Tomoyo is the most suited to being the student body representative.

153
00:09:39,350 --> 00:09:41,720
Vote for Sakagami Tomoyo!

154
00:09:42,600 --> 00:09:46,060
A double event with the Founders Festival
and student council presidential election, eh?

155
00:09:46,520 --> 00:09:48,400
It'll be hectic for a while.

156
00:09:50,400 --> 00:09:51,570
Pay back my Â¥1000.

157
00:09:51,570 --> 00:09:52,150
Eh?

158
00:09:52,570 --> 00:09:55,320
You wasted it, so pay me back in full.

159
00:09:55,860 --> 00:09:57,950
Let me think about that.

160
00:09:58,280 --> 00:09:59,450
You'd <i>better</i>  think about it.

161
00:10:02,950 --> 00:10:06,120
But really, she was a cute girl.

162
00:10:09,580 --> 00:10:11,920
Just think of the Â¥1000 as an investment in her.

163
00:10:12,550 --> 00:10:13,920
Like I will.

164
00:10:23,010 --> 00:10:24,430
I'm having the dream again.

165
00:10:25,560 --> 00:10:28,730
The dream of wandering about, searching for someone.

166
00:10:31,110 --> 00:10:34,070
Then, I finally realize.

167
00:10:35,030 --> 00:10:40,950
I'm just the mind and don't have a body.

168
00:10:42,240 --> 00:10:48,080
That's why that someone didn't notice me, either.

169
00:10:49,920 --> 00:10:53,790
So first, I started to look for my body.

170
00:10:54,960 --> 00:10:58,590
I looked for it in a hurry and in panic.

171
00:10:59,260 --> 00:11:04,180
And I finally found a container for myself.

172
00:11:17,530 --> 00:11:23,620
Even then, I didn't think I'd meet the person anytime soon.

173
00:11:25,830 --> 00:11:27,370
There was no sign the person, either.

174
00:11:30,290 --> 00:11:36,880
Beyond my eyes were endless plains that stretched to the horizon.

175
00:11:40,590 --> 00:11:42,680
Tomoya. Tomoya.

176
00:11:44,300 --> 00:11:47,260
I was able to come home a little earlier than usual.

177
00:11:47,890 --> 00:11:49,520
Should I toast some bread for you?

178
00:11:49,520 --> 00:11:52,230
You should eat something before you go to school.

179
00:11:54,650 --> 00:11:55,360
Tomoya-kun.

180
00:11:56,730 --> 00:11:57,820
I don't need any.

181
00:11:58,360 --> 00:11:59,070
Tomoya.

182
00:12:09,120 --> 00:12:12,210
My mother died when I was five.

183
00:12:13,170 --> 00:12:16,540
I've been raised by my father ever since.

184
00:12:19,710 --> 00:12:24,640
I'm sure it was hard for him to work
and take care of me at the same time.

185
00:12:25,300 --> 00:12:26,890
I understand that well.

186
00:12:27,640 --> 00:12:28,350
But...

187
00:12:30,310 --> 00:12:36,860
But I started having that dream that freezes
my heart before I started elementary school,

188
00:12:37,650 --> 00:12:41,940
and unknowingly, I started not to speak with my father.

189
00:12:44,240 --> 00:12:47,070
On top of that, the fatal accident took place.

190
00:12:50,580 --> 00:12:57,580
It was autumn of my 3rd year of junior high, when admission to a high school through a sports scholarship looked promising.

191
00:13:02,630 --> 00:13:03,630
Tomoya!

192
00:13:04,880 --> 00:13:06,340
I'm home, Tomoya!

193
00:13:06,930 --> 00:13:10,310
Dad's back with a gift!

194
00:13:10,760 --> 00:13:15,100
Come on, eat up. It's the supreme sushi set.

195
00:13:15,100 --> 00:13:16,100
I don't want it.

196
00:13:16,560 --> 00:13:17,440
What?

197
00:13:17,860 --> 00:13:20,270
And you smell sick of alcohol.

198
00:13:21,690 --> 00:13:22,990
Here, just eat.

199
00:13:23,360 --> 00:13:25,200
I said I don't need it!

200
00:13:27,160 --> 00:13:30,030
Tomoya!

201
00:13:37,330 --> 00:13:39,250
Tomoya? Tomoya-kun?

202
00:13:48,340 --> 00:13:50,220
The shoulder tendon is ripped.

203
00:13:51,100 --> 00:13:53,020
The doctor diagnosed it as such...

204
00:13:54,640 --> 00:13:56,560
...and my basketball life ended.

205
00:14:17,660 --> 00:14:18,330
What?

206
00:14:19,000 --> 00:14:20,330
Like I said...

207
00:14:20,330 --> 00:14:21,540
Huh?

208
00:14:21,880 --> 00:14:24,380
Like I said, I wanted to ask for a favor from you again.

209
00:14:24,880 --> 00:14:26,670
"Favor" you say...

210
00:14:27,050 --> 00:14:29,970
Please let me walk up the hill behind you.

211
00:14:34,060 --> 00:14:35,270
We're late again.

212
00:14:35,640 --> 00:14:36,770
It's all right.

213
00:14:37,430 --> 00:14:40,060
If all you need is a back to follow up,
there are plenty of others.

214
00:14:40,440 --> 00:14:41,650
Just ask other people.

215
00:14:43,520 --> 00:14:45,650
Don't tell me you waited for me.

216
00:14:45,650 --> 00:14:46,940
Yes, I was.

217
00:14:47,440 --> 00:14:48,530
You've got to be kidding me.

218
00:14:48,950 --> 00:14:53,030
Okazaki Tomoya-san. I got to know the name.

219
00:14:53,450 --> 00:14:55,290
It's a very ill-intentioned ambush.

220
00:14:55,660 --> 00:14:57,410
Yes, I was ambushing.

221
00:15:06,300 --> 00:15:08,420
The hill's nothing.

222
00:15:08,840 --> 00:15:10,300
Why can't you walk this up alone?

223
00:15:11,180 --> 00:15:12,470
There's nothing...

224
00:15:13,430 --> 00:15:14,100
Nothing?

225
00:15:14,430 --> 00:15:19,600
Even if I went to school, I don't know what I should do.

226
00:15:19,600 --> 00:15:24,400
There is nothing fun...
nor is there a reason I have to be there.

227
00:15:25,150 --> 00:15:28,530
I can't go to a place where I know there's nothing.

228
00:15:29,030 --> 00:15:32,240
I get worried, my legs stop moving, and I shake.

229
00:15:34,780 --> 00:15:36,580
You said you liked the sweet bean bread there.

230
00:15:37,200 --> 00:15:38,160
Yes, it's good.

231
00:15:38,750 --> 00:15:40,830
Then walk up the hill to eat the sweet bean bread.

232
00:15:42,000 --> 00:15:45,170
Yes, I guess... But sweet bean bread isn't enough...

233
00:15:45,630 --> 00:15:47,380
Then find something.

234
00:15:47,380 --> 00:15:50,300
Find something you need to do at school.

235
00:15:51,300 --> 00:15:52,300
Something?

236
00:15:53,140 --> 00:15:54,550
Find that, and then no more ambushing.

237
00:15:56,100 --> 00:15:57,100
See ya.

238
00:16:03,310 --> 00:16:04,810
Furukawa Nagisa.

239
00:16:05,110 --> 00:16:10,690
She's a senior like us, but she's probably a year or two older than us.

240
00:16:12,400 --> 00:16:18,200
She was sick all last year,
so she's repeating her senior year.

241
00:16:18,910 --> 00:16:21,500
No wonder we've never seen her around before.

242
00:16:23,540 --> 00:16:25,710
If you have anything else you want to know, say so.

243
00:16:25,710 --> 00:16:28,590
My information network comes in handy.

244
00:16:30,300 --> 00:16:31,300
What?

245
00:16:31,300 --> 00:16:32,760
Â¥500.

246
00:16:32,760 --> 00:16:33,880
No IOUs.

247
00:16:33,880 --> 00:16:35,840
I never asked.

248
00:16:35,840 --> 00:16:38,810
Oh, no. Your face says you want to know more.

249
00:16:38,810 --> 00:16:39,850
No, it doesn't.

250
00:16:40,720 --> 00:16:42,060
Sunohara Youhei.

251
00:16:42,810 --> 00:16:45,350
Former star midfielder of the soccer team.

252
00:16:45,940 --> 00:16:49,980
Right now, he got booted from the club and is just a punk.

253
00:16:50,570 --> 00:16:54,700
He got in as a sports recruit,
but he snapped in the middle of a game.

254
00:17:17,510 --> 00:17:19,510
I didn't hear what the exact reason was,

255
00:17:19,930 --> 00:17:22,060
but he broke another player's teeth,

256
00:17:22,060 --> 00:17:23,310
bit off an ear,

257
00:17:23,560 --> 00:17:28,360
and he kicked his coach's most important appendage with full power.

258
00:17:37,160 --> 00:17:45,120
He's usually a carefree guy, but he got labeled a monster when he snaps, and now I'm the only one he talks to at school.

259
00:17:45,710 --> 00:17:47,920
No stars out tonight.

260
00:17:50,960 --> 00:17:55,010
By the way, unlike me, he's got guts.

261
00:17:59,430 --> 00:18:04,850
I mean, even after he got booted from the team, he's still living in the dorm.

262
00:18:05,680 --> 00:18:08,560
In the dorm where only sports recruited students can live.

263
00:18:08,850 --> 00:18:15,530
Well, what can I do?! My family's poor,
so I can't find a new apartment now and pay rent!

264
00:18:16,150 --> 00:18:20,990
He brags how he's managed through
the school's multiple attempts to get him out.

265
00:18:25,330 --> 00:18:26,500
I want some ramen.

266
00:18:28,080 --> 00:18:30,880
You bought a big size one, didn't you?

267
00:18:31,710 --> 00:18:34,130
No! This is my breakfast!

268
00:18:34,130 --> 00:18:34,760
You can't have it!

269
00:18:38,090 --> 00:18:42,100
Windy weather lasted for a few days after a rain...

270
00:18:44,260 --> 00:18:46,220
...and that ended the sakura for the year.

271
00:18:49,520 --> 00:18:50,770
Um...

272
00:18:52,230 --> 00:18:53,480
Hey. Haven't seen you in a while.

273
00:18:53,940 --> 00:18:55,980
Yes. It's been a while.

274
00:18:59,200 --> 00:19:02,120
I had a little fever and was absent from school.

275
00:19:02,370 --> 00:19:03,330
I see.

276
00:19:03,700 --> 00:19:04,450
Yes.

277
00:19:08,210 --> 00:19:13,250
But look. I'm better now and am walking up the hill myself.

278
00:19:13,630 --> 00:19:16,000
It's natural to walk up alone.

279
00:19:16,800 --> 00:19:17,460
Yes.

280
00:19:19,340 --> 00:19:22,800
Tomoya-san, I found something at school that I look forward to.

281
00:19:25,010 --> 00:19:27,970
I've thought about it, and I found it.

282
00:19:29,270 --> 00:19:30,140
That's good.

283
00:19:30,140 --> 00:19:30,810
Yes.

284
00:19:32,650 --> 00:19:34,440
Thank you very much.

285
00:19:34,440 --> 00:19:36,190
It's all due to your advice.

286
00:19:36,190 --> 00:19:38,110
I didn't do anything.

287
00:19:45,660 --> 00:19:46,830
What?

288
00:19:46,830 --> 00:19:48,120
Oh, nothing.

289
00:20:13,650 --> 00:20:14,770
Hello.

290
00:20:19,900 --> 00:20:21,240
I did it!

291
00:20:22,490 --> 00:20:25,120
Hey, I did it!

292
00:20:25,120 --> 00:20:27,280
I was able to buy stuffed bread today!

293
00:20:27,950 --> 00:20:31,000
Look, dumpling sandwich and fried noodle bread.

294
00:20:34,290 --> 00:20:36,170
Hello.

295
00:20:37,000 --> 00:20:38,340
What is this?

296
00:20:38,750 --> 00:20:39,880
What are you doing?

297
00:20:42,090 --> 00:20:46,010
Furukawa, if stuffed bread is all right, come stuff yourself.

298
00:20:46,010 --> 00:20:47,470
Just kidding.

299
00:20:48,390 --> 00:20:51,390
Tatata, tada!

300
00:20:53,850 --> 00:20:54,730
What is this?

301
00:20:55,480 --> 00:20:57,690
Recruiting members?

302
00:20:57,690 --> 00:20:58,900
The Theater Club?!

303
00:20:59,110 --> 00:21:01,400
Yes. I'm recruiting members.

304
00:21:01,650 --> 00:21:06,110
I will reestablish the Theater Club that closed down last year because all the members left.

305
00:21:06,490 --> 00:21:10,080
I'm making a poster for that.

306
00:21:10,910 --> 00:21:12,910
Theater Club, eh?

307
00:21:12,910 --> 00:21:16,630
This... This drawing looks like a marshmallow, if not an egg.

308
00:21:16,630 --> 00:21:17,380
What is it?

309
00:21:17,670 --> 00:21:19,380
It's the Big Dango Family.

310
00:21:19,380 --> 00:21:23,010
It's the Big Dango Family that was popular when I was a child.

311
00:21:23,010 --> 00:21:24,930
I drew them since I love them.

312
00:21:25,300 --> 00:21:29,390
Dango, dango, dango, dango.

313
00:21:29,390 --> 00:21:33,310
Dango family is a big family.

314
00:21:33,310 --> 00:21:40,020
Always a happy big family.

315
00:21:40,020 --> 00:21:43,860
The house is always like a sports day.

316
00:21:44,110 --> 00:21:47,860
Ready go, run run run. Family marathon.

317
00:21:48,240 --> 00:21:51,830
Time for a bath. Get inside. Breath-holding competition.

318
00:21:51,830 --> 00:21:56,670
Dango. Dango's a big family.

319
00:21:57,080 --> 00:22:01,130
Oh yeah, I remember that song back when I was a kid.

320
00:22:01,670 --> 00:22:05,380
The boom still lives within me.

321
00:22:05,380 --> 00:22:09,090
The big family where everyone cares about each other.

322
00:22:09,340 --> 00:22:10,470
I love them so much.

323
00:22:11,050 --> 00:22:16,230
So, this Theater Club is what you mentioned earlier...

324
00:22:16,230 --> 00:22:20,190
Yes. It's the fun I found at school.

325
00:22:20,730 --> 00:22:22,770
I will reestablish the Theater Club.

326
00:22:22,770 --> 00:22:26,700
I will perform a play at the Founders Festival.

327
00:22:27,450 --> 00:22:31,410
I think I'll be able to walk up
the hill every day if I have this goal.

328
00:22:33,740 --> 00:22:38,580
Anyway, I'll make lots of posters
and post them everywhere around the school.

329
00:22:39,620 --> 00:22:44,130
Dango, dango, dango, dango.

330
00:22:44,130 --> 00:22:48,680
Dango family is a big family.

331
00:22:48,680 --> 00:22:55,220
Always a happy big family.

332
00:22:49,630 --> 00:22:55,600
She was singing so cheerfully.

333
00:22:58,810 --> 00:23:04,070
What was that bright light I saw eight years ago on the rooftop about?

334
00:23:06,820 --> 00:23:09,110
Saito Electrical Construction, Ltd.

335
00:23:07,400 --> 00:23:09,240
Hey, Okazaki.

336
00:23:12,910 --> 00:23:13,620
Get in.

337
00:23:13,950 --> 00:23:15,080
You'll catch a cold.

338
00:23:19,000 --> 00:23:21,630
Come back to work already.

339
00:23:22,040 --> 00:23:26,050
It might help you getting over things if you work up a sweat.

340
00:23:26,050 --> 00:23:28,090
I'm sorry, Yoshino-senpai.

341
00:23:28,720 --> 00:23:31,470
Don't worry. You're not being treated as absent without permission.

342
00:23:32,050 --> 00:23:35,430
I'm telling the president that you call in every day.

343
00:23:36,180 --> 00:23:37,310
I'm sorry.

344
00:23:37,890 --> 00:23:38,890
I'll need some more time.

345
00:23:39,680 --> 00:23:42,350
I see. Okay.

346
00:23:43,060 --> 00:23:44,310
I'm sorry.

347
00:23:45,150 --> 00:23:46,820
Everyone's worried about you.

348
00:23:48,490 --> 00:23:50,570
They're all thinking that you're depressed again.

349
00:23:53,950 --> 00:23:57,160
They're all waiting to hear from you.

350
00:23:57,740 --> 00:23:59,790
Everyone's thinking about you.

351
00:24:00,660 --> 00:24:01,870
I'm sorry.

352
00:24:02,210 --> 00:24:04,040
Nagisa-chan often said,

353
00:24:04,630 --> 00:24:07,670
"Big families always think about each other."

354
00:24:08,420 --> 00:24:09,550
I'm sorry!

355
00:24:10,170 --> 00:24:11,130
Okazaki!

356
00:24:14,090 --> 00:24:15,390
Okazaki!

357
00:24:33,950 --> 00:24:35,370
What? What's wrong?

358
00:24:36,320 --> 00:24:37,080
Come with me!

359
00:24:37,330 --> 00:24:38,490
What? To where?

360
00:24:39,040 --> 00:24:39,950
Just come!

361
00:24:45,710 --> 00:24:47,340
That! Take a look.

362
00:24:54,470 --> 00:24:55,590
Void?

363
00:24:55,590 --> 00:24:56,590
What do you mean void?

364
00:24:56,850 --> 00:24:59,720
Void means void. It means invalid.

365
00:25:00,350 --> 00:25:03,310
Member recruitment for clubs was only allowed until last week.

366
00:25:03,310 --> 00:25:07,190
Therefore member recruiting outside of the timeframe is against the rules.

367
00:25:07,860 --> 00:25:09,150
Sakagami.

368
00:25:09,520 --> 00:25:14,280
This forceful act had to have been done by the current student council's executives.

369
00:25:14,280 --> 00:25:16,110
They're eggheads.

370
00:25:16,490 --> 00:25:17,570
Sakagami!

371
00:25:17,570 --> 00:25:21,660
Wh-Where are these executives?!

372
00:25:22,080 --> 00:25:22,950
I don't know.

373
00:25:23,830 --> 00:25:26,120
This poster is handmade, you know?!

374
00:25:26,120 --> 00:25:29,630
It's a message from the heart,
drawn with heart and passion!

375
00:25:30,420 --> 00:25:31,760
Damn this cross!

376
00:25:32,090 --> 00:25:36,630
Guys are strolling around campus looking for these posters.

377
00:25:36,630 --> 00:25:39,220
So they can put the cross on or rip them off walls.

378
00:25:41,810 --> 00:25:44,100
Okazaki! Let's go!

379
00:25:49,360 --> 00:25:50,190
Sunohara!

380
00:25:50,650 --> 00:25:51,860
Don't snap!

381
00:25:51,860 --> 00:25:53,820
If you do, you'll get expelled this time!

382
00:25:56,280 --> 00:25:57,320
Let's go check this out!

383
00:25:57,320 --> 00:25:57,910
Yeah.

384
00:25:57,910 --> 00:25:58,820
He's seriously snapped.

385
00:25:58,820 --> 00:25:59,950
This is interesting.

386
00:26:00,870 --> 00:26:02,450
Come on, let's go.

387
00:26:10,460 --> 00:26:12,710
They got this one, too.

388
00:26:19,550 --> 00:26:21,050
Crap, even here.

389
00:26:21,850 --> 00:26:22,890
Damn it!

390
00:26:28,810 --> 00:26:29,480
Furukawa.

391
00:26:29,770 --> 00:26:32,400
Okazaki! This way!

392
00:26:33,150 --> 00:26:34,730
Meet me on the roof after school!

393
00:26:35,280 --> 00:26:35,860
Yes.

394
00:26:37,650 --> 00:26:38,990
Wait for me on the roof!

395
00:26:39,700 --> 00:26:40,490
Yes...

396
00:26:47,120 --> 00:26:49,170
Hey, hey, hey, hey, hey, hey!

397
00:26:49,670 --> 00:26:51,750
Stop right there!

398
00:27:06,350 --> 00:27:07,310
It's started!

399
00:27:07,560 --> 00:27:09,350
They're over at the old school building.

400
00:27:09,560 --> 00:27:11,690
I heard blood is all over the place already.

401
00:27:11,690 --> 00:27:12,610
Where are they?

402
00:27:12,610 --> 00:27:14,320
This way! Hurry!

403
00:27:14,690 --> 00:27:16,610
What are you doing?

404
00:27:17,070 --> 00:27:21,530
What are <i>you</i>  guys doing to a poster someone drew?!

405
00:27:21,530 --> 00:27:24,740
We were only committing fair warning on illegal posters!

406
00:27:25,120 --> 00:27:27,160
Warning? Fair?!

407
00:27:27,160 --> 00:27:28,120
Don't give me that shit!

408
00:27:28,120 --> 00:27:29,500
You guys are the illegal ones!

409
00:27:29,750 --> 00:27:32,210
How are we illegal?

410
00:27:32,460 --> 00:27:33,670
Like this!

411
00:27:33,920 --> 00:27:34,920
And this!

412
00:27:34,920 --> 00:27:36,550
And this, too!

413
00:27:40,970 --> 00:27:42,090
Take that.

414
00:27:43,180 --> 00:27:45,350
What are you all doing?

415
00:27:46,680 --> 00:27:48,140
The lunch break is already over.

416
00:27:48,390 --> 00:27:50,440
Go back to your classes already.

417
00:27:51,310 --> 00:27:54,150
Keep your hands off of me!

418
00:28:15,500 --> 00:28:17,630
Everyone, leave.

419
00:28:17,960 --> 00:28:19,710
Don't be late for your classes.

420
00:28:19,710 --> 00:28:21,510
Yes.

421
00:28:24,680 --> 00:28:28,890
I don't know what the cause was,
but you have to talk first, Sunohara-kun.

422
00:28:28,890 --> 00:28:30,020
Yes.

423
00:28:30,930 --> 00:28:32,390
Return to your class now.

424
00:28:32,940 --> 00:28:34,060
Yes...

425
00:28:36,270 --> 00:28:37,610
That was a surprise.

426
00:28:37,940 --> 00:28:42,030
I heard there was teacher who practices aikido and teaches second year classes.

427
00:28:42,030 --> 00:28:44,030
It has to be her. What a surprise.

428
00:28:44,410 --> 00:28:46,570
If I'm right, her name was...

429
00:28:47,080 --> 00:28:48,080
Ibuki!

430
00:28:48,080 --> 00:28:49,490
Ibuki Kouko!

431
00:28:51,370 --> 00:28:54,000
Cool girls like her are right in my strike zone.

432
00:28:55,330 --> 00:28:56,290
You perv.

433
00:29:07,930 --> 00:29:10,220
How many did you draw in total?

434
00:29:12,930 --> 00:29:14,770
Fourteen.

435
00:29:15,230 --> 00:29:19,730
I see. Some of them either got
thrown away or taken away by them.

436
00:29:22,530 --> 00:29:24,280
I collected all the ones that I could find.

437
00:29:25,110 --> 00:29:27,700
What a horrible thing they did.

438
00:29:28,240 --> 00:29:29,490
I'm all right.

439
00:29:30,450 --> 00:29:31,620
"All right"?

440
00:29:32,120 --> 00:29:33,120
Furukawa...

441
00:29:33,370 --> 00:29:36,870
I'm all right. I'll draw them again.

442
00:29:36,870 --> 00:29:39,040
I'll draw them again and post them everywhere on campus.

443
00:29:39,420 --> 00:29:41,500
You can't. They'll get you again!

444
00:29:41,880 --> 00:29:44,970
They put the cross and the void sign again.

445
00:29:45,260 --> 00:29:50,180
But I already made up my mind that I'll reestablish the Theater Club.

446
00:29:50,560 --> 00:29:53,640
I never knew there was a deadline on the recruiting period.

447
00:29:54,230 --> 00:29:59,360
Three! If there are three members, it gets acknowledged as a club.

448
00:29:59,360 --> 00:30:00,270
Furukawa...

449
00:30:00,650 --> 00:30:02,730
I'll draw the posters!

450
00:30:02,730 --> 00:30:06,320
I'm sure there are people who want to join the Theater Club.

451
00:30:06,320 --> 00:30:07,240
There have to be!

452
00:30:07,740 --> 00:30:10,950
Furukawa, why do you want to do theater so much?

453
00:30:13,160 --> 00:30:14,120
Why?

454
00:30:15,750 --> 00:30:19,460
I can't tell you the reason now.

455
00:30:20,080 --> 00:30:20,920
But...

456
00:30:20,920 --> 00:30:23,090
But I want to do it.

457
00:30:24,340 --> 00:30:27,680
Okay, then go draw the poster.

458
00:30:30,260 --> 00:30:33,180
A really amazing one, but just one will do.

459
00:30:33,180 --> 00:30:34,640
We'll photocopy it.

460
00:30:34,640 --> 00:30:37,390
We'll make a hundred or two hundred copies of it.

461
00:30:37,390 --> 00:30:39,900
Then Sunohara and I will post them all around the school.

462
00:30:41,150 --> 00:30:42,360
Photocopy...

463
00:30:42,610 --> 00:30:45,150
That's it, Okazaki! That's the way to go!

464
00:30:45,570 --> 00:30:49,240
All right, leave it to us. If they're just copies, no matter how many crosses they make,

465
00:30:49,450 --> 00:30:51,740
we'll just post up more from over them!

466
00:30:54,160 --> 00:30:55,200
This is a war!

467
00:30:55,200 --> 00:30:58,040
I'll take this to the extreme against the student council executives!

468
00:31:00,580 --> 00:31:04,380
War, eh? That's not very peaceful.

469
00:31:08,420 --> 00:31:10,180
Sensei, here she is.

470
00:31:18,680 --> 00:31:19,350
It's her.

471
00:31:20,230 --> 00:31:23,820
This Furukawa-san is you, right?

472
00:31:24,520 --> 00:31:25,820
Ibuki-sensei.

473
00:31:27,150 --> 00:31:28,400
Furukawa, you know her?

474
00:31:28,990 --> 00:31:33,370
She was the advisor of the
Theater Club before it closed down.

475
00:31:33,370 --> 00:31:35,330
I-I see.

476
00:31:38,960 --> 00:31:41,670
Furukawa-san, you're interested in theater?

477
00:31:42,210 --> 00:31:46,130
Yes. I filled out the member form once before.

478
00:31:46,630 --> 00:31:47,880
Oh, you did?

479
00:31:48,840 --> 00:31:53,890
But I couldn't come to school soon after
and had to be absent from school for the entire year,

480
00:31:54,350 --> 00:31:56,680
and the club was closed down while I was gone.

481
00:31:57,640 --> 00:31:59,310
I see.

482
00:32:00,270 --> 00:32:00,940
Yes.

483
00:32:01,850 --> 00:32:04,020
Then, if the club is reestablished...

484
00:32:04,610 --> 00:32:06,020
I'd be very happy.

485
00:32:07,190 --> 00:32:12,570
It is past the deadline, but if you can get members together, I'll talk to the school.

486
00:32:12,570 --> 00:32:14,320
You mean that?

487
00:32:14,740 --> 00:32:16,370
So keep at it.

488
00:32:17,450 --> 00:32:18,290
Yes!

489
00:32:38,060 --> 00:32:41,520
The plan ended in failure.

490
00:32:45,730 --> 00:32:47,400
No one wanted to join.

491
00:32:47,690 --> 00:32:49,980
The reestablishment of the
Theater Club was going to end in vain...

492
00:32:49,980 --> 00:32:50,990
...or was supposed to have.

493
00:32:51,400 --> 00:32:53,150
There's nothing we can do, Furukawa.

494
00:32:53,950 --> 00:32:56,160
This world favors comedy.

495
00:32:56,160 --> 00:32:58,160
Serious stuff don't get much attention.

496
00:32:59,040 --> 00:33:02,120
We did what we can, so we have to face the results, right?

497
00:33:02,500 --> 00:33:03,920
Right, Okazaki?

498
00:33:03,920 --> 00:33:05,580
Huh? Yeah.

499
00:33:07,920 --> 00:33:10,210
The poster was good, you know.

500
00:33:10,840 --> 00:33:13,720
Nagisa kept working.

501
00:33:14,300 --> 00:33:16,340
She used an amazing secret trick.

502
00:33:16,720 --> 00:33:17,850
She worked really hard.

503
00:33:21,720 --> 00:33:23,270
Wh-Wha?

504
00:33:23,270 --> 00:33:25,390
H-Hold on a minute, Furukawa.

505
00:33:27,610 --> 00:33:30,520
I'll have you two fill out the member form.

506
00:33:30,780 --> 00:33:34,450
Then that makes three including me.

507
00:33:34,450 --> 00:33:35,360
Furukawa!

508
00:33:36,030 --> 00:33:38,120
Then everything will be solved.

509
00:33:38,490 --> 00:33:43,580
The Theater Club will have Ibuki-sensei as the advisor and will restart.

510
00:33:45,080 --> 00:33:47,540
Sorry Furukawa. I can't do that.

511
00:33:48,830 --> 00:33:50,750
I'm not going to participate in a club.

512
00:33:51,130 --> 00:33:53,460
Yeah. We're staying away from clubs!

513
00:33:54,010 --> 00:33:57,890
Both Okazaki and I are able to be who we are because we aren't in any clubs!

514
00:33:58,340 --> 00:34:01,350
Besides, I'm not into acting.

515
00:34:01,510 --> 00:34:02,770
Like water and oil!

516
00:34:02,770 --> 00:34:04,180
He's a basketball man,

517
00:34:04,180 --> 00:34:06,770
and I was once called the soccer prodigy.

518
00:34:06,770 --> 00:34:09,060
Yes, I know, it's about the past.

519
00:34:09,730 --> 00:34:13,990
In other words, screaming "You idiot" at the sunset,

520
00:34:14,900 --> 00:34:17,860
or saying "I love you. J-J-Ju-Ju..."

521
00:34:17,860 --> 00:34:22,030
for a love scene are total mismatches for us!

522
00:34:22,030 --> 00:34:23,830
We don't comprehend that kind of language!

523
00:34:24,660 --> 00:34:25,790
Are you fine with this argument?

524
00:34:25,790 --> 00:34:26,660
Huh? Yeah.

525
00:34:27,250 --> 00:34:29,130
Do you understand?!

526
00:34:41,600 --> 00:34:43,470
Stop giggling.

527
00:34:44,970 --> 00:34:48,310
Please donât worry too much.

528
00:34:48,020 --> 00:34:49,600
It'll be fine.

529
00:34:49,600 --> 00:34:51,900
Fine? What about?

530
00:34:51,900 --> 00:34:57,360
I plan on doing a solo play on the Founders Festival's stage.

531
00:34:57,360 --> 00:34:59,530
Solo play?

532
00:34:59,530 --> 00:35:05,750
I won't ask either of you to stand on the stage or recite lines.

533
00:35:06,620 --> 00:35:09,170
I promise-

534
00:35:09,920 --> 00:35:10,880
Found it!

535
00:35:12,170 --> 00:35:13,380
Excuse me.

536
00:35:13,790 --> 00:35:20,180
Um... Um... That's Dangos on a Stick from the Big Dango Family series, right?

537
00:35:20,180 --> 00:35:22,640
Yes. You know your stuff.

538
00:35:22,640 --> 00:35:23,640
You're exactly right.

539
00:35:23,640 --> 00:35:26,390
I've been searching for it. I'll have it.

540
00:35:26,930 --> 00:35:31,850
Oh, but I don't have money on me, so may I come get it tomorrow after school?

541
00:35:31,850 --> 00:35:33,270
Sure, that's fine.

542
00:35:33,270 --> 00:35:36,030
That's great. I'm so happy.

543
00:35:36,030 --> 00:35:39,780
Please don't sell it until then.

544
00:35:39,780 --> 00:35:44,080
Don't worry. The boom was long ago.

545
00:35:44,080 --> 00:35:46,370
Nobody wants it now.

546
00:35:46,370 --> 00:35:50,750
You can take it with you today. Come pay me tomorrow.

547
00:35:51,500 --> 00:35:52,790
Really?

548
00:35:52,790 --> 00:35:54,210
Thank you very much!

549
00:35:54,210 --> 00:35:58,460
Dango, dango, dango, dango.

550
00:35:58,460 --> 00:36:02,680
Dango family is a big family.

551
00:36:02,680 --> 00:36:08,850
Always a happy big family.

552
00:36:02,680 --> 00:36:05,430
That was the extent of our resistance.

553
00:36:06,390 --> 00:36:10,430
We were signed up to the club, going with the flow.

554
00:36:11,480 --> 00:36:13,020
With the flow...

555
00:36:13,690 --> 00:36:18,150
I guess that was very much alike me.

556
00:36:22,200 --> 00:36:25,870
And, like always, after I get carried with the flow,

557
00:36:26,490 --> 00:36:28,700
I'll regret it later.

558
00:36:32,040 --> 00:36:33,120
A solo play.

559
00:36:34,000 --> 00:36:36,380
That sounds good.

560
00:36:37,170 --> 00:36:43,760
It's very suitable for this small Theater Club that has just started.

561
00:36:43,760 --> 00:36:46,970
"Small", eh? She's right.

562
00:36:46,970 --> 00:36:48,680
So small.

563
00:36:48,680 --> 00:36:51,020
What will the scenario be?

564
00:36:51,020 --> 00:36:53,600
Yes, I'll work on it.

565
00:36:56,360 --> 00:36:57,520
What play are you going to perform?

566
00:36:57,520 --> 00:36:59,020
On what play will you base it on?

567
00:36:59,440 --> 00:37:03,150
There are many to choose from, like Shakespeare or Baudelaire's poems.

568
00:37:03,150 --> 00:37:06,120
No, um... It'll be an original work.

569
00:37:06,740 --> 00:37:07,950
Original?

570
00:37:07,950 --> 00:37:09,330
Your own?

571
00:37:10,160 --> 00:37:11,160
Yes.

572
00:37:11,160 --> 00:37:13,960
I see. I can't wait to see it.

573
00:37:14,710 --> 00:37:15,330
Yes.

574
00:37:16,250 --> 00:37:20,590
We're less than a month before the
Founders Festival, so you have much to work on.

575
00:37:21,050 --> 00:37:21,800
Yes.

576
00:37:22,300 --> 00:37:24,880
I'll help you out anytime you need assistance.

577
00:37:25,430 --> 00:37:26,260
Yes.

578
00:37:27,640 --> 00:37:29,680
Okay then, stage crew boys.

579
00:37:31,810 --> 00:37:37,610
This room will be the club room starting today,
so sort out the necessary and unnecessary things.

580
00:37:39,570 --> 00:37:41,440
Where's your answer?

581
00:37:42,030 --> 00:37:43,400
Yes!

582
00:37:43,650 --> 00:37:47,280
That concludes the first new Theater Club's meeting.

583
00:37:47,740 --> 00:37:49,740
Good luck everyone.

584
00:37:50,080 --> 00:37:52,330
She said we're the stage crew.

585
00:37:52,660 --> 00:37:54,460
Looks like we are now.

586
00:37:55,000 --> 00:38:00,380
I had a brighter image of a Theater Club, but I guess shadows exist everywhere.

587
00:38:00,750 --> 00:38:02,250
Can't agree more.

588
00:38:02,510 --> 00:38:04,470
I'll help out as well.

589
00:38:09,140 --> 00:38:09,970
Your house?!

590
00:38:10,850 --> 00:38:11,970
Yes.

591
00:38:12,470 --> 00:38:13,930
Your house, eh...

592
00:38:13,930 --> 00:38:15,480
Yes, my house.

593
00:38:16,020 --> 00:38:17,850
Why your house?

594
00:38:18,270 --> 00:38:20,810
I'm saying, please join me for dinner.

595
00:38:20,810 --> 00:38:22,190
Then we'll have a meeting.

596
00:38:22,730 --> 00:38:23,650
Dinner?

597
00:38:23,980 --> 00:38:24,900
Meeting?

598
00:38:25,190 --> 00:38:32,330
I need to write the script, and I'm sure you two need to work out your schedules with this new commitment.

599
00:38:32,330 --> 00:38:34,160
Who cares about working out schedules?

600
00:38:34,160 --> 00:38:35,580
Do it yourself.

601
00:38:35,580 --> 00:38:39,290
I don't know anything about scenario and stuff, and I'm not interested in it.

602
00:38:39,290 --> 00:38:40,000
But dinner...

603
00:38:40,330 --> 00:38:43,090
I can't go to other people's house just to go eat dinner!

604
00:38:43,090 --> 00:38:45,710
Convenience store food matches my stomach best.

605
00:38:45,710 --> 00:38:46,590
Right, Sunohara?

606
00:38:47,630 --> 00:38:48,630
Hey, Sunohara!

607
00:38:48,630 --> 00:38:51,220
Sorry, I have something to take care of today!

608
00:38:53,060 --> 00:38:54,430
Bye!

609
00:38:57,430 --> 00:38:58,770
Stop, you!

610
00:38:59,690 --> 00:39:01,650
You plan on leaving me at a time like this?

611
00:39:01,980 --> 00:39:03,570
No, I seriously have business to take care of.

612
00:39:03,900 --> 00:39:05,780
Stop screwing around with me.

613
00:39:05,780 --> 00:39:06,650
I have a part-time job.

614
00:39:07,400 --> 00:39:08,240
Part-time job?

615
00:39:11,740 --> 00:39:15,160
I heard my house's doing horrible financially.

616
00:39:15,160 --> 00:39:17,500
My monthly allowance hasn't been sent to me in a while.

617
00:39:17,870 --> 00:39:22,460
I know what it's like right now,
but I've decided to pick up a job. Three times a week.

618
00:39:23,130 --> 00:39:27,420
A senpai... A senpai from our school hooked me up.

619
00:39:29,090 --> 00:39:29,880
I see.

620
00:39:30,180 --> 00:39:33,180
Today's the first day. I don't want to be late.

621
00:39:33,180 --> 00:39:33,930
Bye.

622
00:39:34,510 --> 00:39:35,430
Sunohara.

623
00:39:37,180 --> 00:39:39,520
Sorry I stopped you.

624
00:39:40,230 --> 00:39:41,100
Do your best.

625
00:39:58,040 --> 00:39:59,710
Your house is a bakery?

626
00:40:00,160 --> 00:40:03,290
Furukawa Bread is famous around here.

627
00:40:05,210 --> 00:40:06,250
I'm home.

628
00:40:09,130 --> 00:40:10,800
Welcome home, Nagisa.

629
00:40:11,300 --> 00:40:12,640
Welcome.

630
00:40:12,640 --> 00:40:15,100
Oh? I had heard you were bringing two guests.

631
00:40:15,100 --> 00:40:16,010
There's only one.

632
00:40:16,010 --> 00:40:19,520
I get it! He must be Okazaki Tomoya-san.

633
00:40:19,520 --> 00:40:21,060
You guessed right, Mom.

634
00:40:21,600 --> 00:40:25,230
Of course I can tell; he's exactly as you described.

635
00:40:25,650 --> 00:40:28,690
How did she describe me?

636
00:40:28,980 --> 00:40:32,110
Shh. You can't, Mom. We promised you wouldn't tell.

637
00:40:32,490 --> 00:40:34,700
Therefore, I can't tell you.

638
00:40:35,410 --> 00:40:36,780
Where's Dad?

639
00:40:36,780 --> 00:40:37,790
Over at the park.

640
00:40:37,790 --> 00:40:41,000
Playing baseball with the children
from the neighborhood like always.

641
00:40:41,000 --> 00:40:42,250
Ah, baseball.

642
00:40:42,250 --> 00:40:43,750
Yes, baseball.

643
00:40:46,750 --> 00:40:49,050
You must be Okazaki Tomoya.

644
00:40:49,050 --> 00:40:52,220
You've been sucking up to Nagisa and finally made your way into our house.

645
00:40:52,510 --> 00:40:54,970
No, um... I never...

646
00:40:55,220 --> 00:40:56,930
If you're a man, then fight me!

647
00:40:56,930 --> 00:40:57,890
Come to the park!

648
00:40:58,430 --> 00:40:59,680
Dad...

649
00:40:59,680 --> 00:41:02,140
Don't worry.

650
00:41:02,770 --> 00:41:04,770
Dinner will be ready soon.

651
00:41:05,350 --> 00:41:07,230
I know.

652
00:41:10,900 --> 00:41:14,860
What are you doing, Okazaki?!
Catch it with everything you've got!

653
00:41:15,490 --> 00:41:16,530
Life is...

654
00:41:17,070 --> 00:41:18,700
...about fights!

655
00:41:18,700 --> 00:41:20,790
The moment you let down your guard...

656
00:41:20,790 --> 00:41:25,210
...you get stamped as a loser!

657
00:41:32,170 --> 00:41:33,260
Hey!

658
00:41:33,970 --> 00:41:35,970
I've never played baseball before.

659
00:41:36,390 --> 00:41:37,510
I'm not interested in it, either.

660
00:41:39,600 --> 00:41:41,970
Just throw the ball back already.

661
00:41:42,890 --> 00:41:47,650
If I catch the ball you throw,
I can judge how big a man you are.

662
00:41:48,650 --> 00:41:49,570
"How big"?

663
00:41:49,980 --> 00:41:52,150
Big as in how?

664
00:41:53,240 --> 00:41:56,950
A, B+, or C-.

665
00:41:56,950 --> 00:42:00,030
I'm judging if you're suitable for Nagisa or not.

666
00:42:00,030 --> 00:42:02,410
I don't want you making judgments on me!

667
00:42:03,040 --> 00:42:05,750
Don't get out of the way this time!

668
00:42:11,960 --> 00:42:14,130
Good! Now throw it back!

669
00:42:29,900 --> 00:42:32,650
Why don't you throw it back properly?!

670
00:42:33,650 --> 00:42:35,490
The tendon in my shoulder's torn,

671
00:42:35,940 --> 00:42:38,610
so my right arm can only go up this high.

672
00:42:44,620 --> 00:42:47,830
Akio-san! Dinner's ready!

673
00:42:47,830 --> 00:42:49,370
Coming.

674
00:42:49,750 --> 00:42:52,840
Akio-san, has the shirataki absorbed enough flavor?

675
00:42:53,090 --> 00:42:55,710
Yes, it's the best. Sanae-chan's the best cook.

676
00:42:55,710 --> 00:42:57,090
You are the iron chef.

677
00:42:57,090 --> 00:42:58,550
A hottie on top of that, too.

678
00:42:59,010 --> 00:43:00,930
Akio-san, you have rice on your face.

679
00:43:00,340 --> 00:43:02,350
Take it off for me.

680
00:43:02,470 --> 00:43:05,720
Hey, it's almost strange how well your parents get along.

681
00:43:03,060 --> 00:43:04,310
They're off now.

682
00:43:04,310 --> 00:43:05,720
Thank you.

683
00:43:06,230 --> 00:43:07,730
They're always like this.

684
00:43:08,100 --> 00:43:08,890
Always?

685
00:43:09,270 --> 00:43:11,690
Here, Sanae-chan. Say "Ah".

686
00:43:11,690 --> 00:43:12,650
Ah~

687
00:43:13,770 --> 00:43:16,110
It's not "almost". They are strange.

688
00:43:17,190 --> 00:43:19,320
Tomoya-san. Say "Ah".

689
00:43:19,320 --> 00:43:20,450
You've got to be kidding me.

690
00:43:20,450 --> 00:43:22,450
How about some, Okazaki?

691
00:43:23,030 --> 00:43:23,910
Yes, thank you.

692
00:43:25,240 --> 00:43:27,410
You're still in high school, remember that.

693
00:43:29,410 --> 00:43:30,960
Akio-san, you're so mean.

694
00:43:31,500 --> 00:43:34,380
But, Sanae-chan loves Akio-san.

695
00:43:34,380 --> 00:43:36,420
Yes, I do.

696
00:43:36,800 --> 00:43:38,300
I can't take this.

697
00:43:38,880 --> 00:43:40,630
Hey, grumpy face.

698
00:43:41,470 --> 00:43:42,800
Want one?

699
00:43:43,390 --> 00:43:44,510
Don't mind me if I do.

700
00:43:46,430 --> 00:43:48,140
He fell for it again.

701
00:43:49,770 --> 00:43:51,940
Oh, Akio-san.

702
00:43:57,480 --> 00:44:00,030
Aw, that felt good.

703
00:44:03,410 --> 00:44:06,240
Hey, you two go take a shower.

704
00:44:10,910 --> 00:44:14,210
Of course I was joking!

705
00:44:15,130 --> 00:44:16,670
Scenario?

706
00:44:17,090 --> 00:44:19,050
Yes, scenario.

707
00:44:19,300 --> 00:44:23,470
But I don't hear a thing coming from Nagisa's room.

708
00:44:23,470 --> 00:44:26,260
Of course, since she's working on the scenario.

709
00:44:28,930 --> 00:44:33,150
What kind of plot is this original story going to have?

710
00:44:36,110 --> 00:44:38,480
I'm sorry, what was that, Tomoya-san?

711
00:44:38,480 --> 00:44:41,780
Nothing. Go ahead and keep working. Don't mind me.

712
00:44:41,780 --> 00:44:44,240
Okay. Then I'll continue.

713
00:44:48,870 --> 00:44:51,500
You own a lot of the Big Dango Family, eh?

714
00:44:51,960 --> 00:44:54,500
Actually, there is more than this out there.

715
00:44:55,130 --> 00:44:57,090
I will collect them all one day.

716
00:44:59,710 --> 00:45:00,760
All right.

717
00:45:00,760 --> 00:45:02,260
I'll should get myself out of here.

718
00:45:04,220 --> 00:45:06,430
This is one of Akio-san's old pajamas.

719
00:45:06,430 --> 00:45:07,300
Go ahead and use it.

720
00:45:07,970 --> 00:45:10,350
Oh no. I'm leaving now.

721
00:45:10,720 --> 00:45:13,560
Oh, you weren't planning on staying over?

722
00:45:14,810 --> 00:45:17,310
I never intended to.

723
00:45:17,310 --> 00:45:19,400
Just stay.

724
00:45:19,780 --> 00:45:20,730
No...

725
00:45:20,730 --> 00:45:26,030
As a fellow Theater Club member, you plan on leaving Nagisa, who might end up pulling an all-nighter, alone?

726
00:45:26,030 --> 00:45:26,740
N-No...

727
00:45:26,740 --> 00:45:29,160
Then stay.

728
00:45:29,740 --> 00:45:30,490
Okay.

729
00:45:32,000 --> 00:45:34,620
Don't worry; you'll be sharing a bed with me.

730
00:45:34,620 --> 00:45:35,250
Eh?

731
00:45:35,250 --> 00:45:36,330
You got problem with that?

732
00:45:36,330 --> 00:45:37,210
Yes.

733
00:45:37,210 --> 00:45:39,590
Want me to lock you in a figure-four?

734
00:46:05,110 --> 00:46:06,320
You can't sleep?

735
00:46:06,320 --> 00:46:08,280
No. You can't either?

736
00:46:09,530 --> 00:46:11,620
My reason is obvious.

737
00:46:11,620 --> 00:46:14,410
I'm basically sleeping with a wild animal in the same cage.

738
00:46:15,540 --> 00:46:17,540
Dad's snoring must be keeping you up.

739
00:46:17,540 --> 00:46:19,130
Yeah, exactly.

740
00:46:19,880 --> 00:46:22,670
I heard Mom got used to it soon enough.

741
00:46:23,800 --> 00:46:26,510
If you listen to it closely, she says it's cute.

742
00:46:28,470 --> 00:46:31,010
What does it take to hear that?

743
00:46:32,510 --> 00:46:35,560
You smiled. Tomoya-san smiled.

744
00:46:35,560 --> 00:46:36,850
No, I didn't.

745
00:46:36,850 --> 00:46:40,770
Tomoya-san, who always has a grumpy face, smiled.

746
00:46:40,770 --> 00:46:41,480
Be quiet.

747
00:46:42,820 --> 00:46:45,690
You have a very kind face when you smile.

748
00:46:47,360 --> 00:46:48,740
I'm sorry.

749
00:46:53,910 --> 00:46:58,000
I know what I should write.

750
00:46:58,000 --> 00:47:02,000
But I can't write it well, so I can't go to sleep.

751
00:47:02,340 --> 00:47:05,880
Also, I'm happy to have you close to me.

752
00:47:06,880 --> 00:47:11,390
I'm so happy, so it feels like a waste to go to bed.

753
00:47:15,180 --> 00:47:16,220
I'm sorry.

754
00:47:19,100 --> 00:47:22,060
Dream... It's about a dream.

755
00:47:22,270 --> 00:47:27,530
It's about the dream that I've been having since I was little and am still having.

756
00:47:27,900 --> 00:47:29,780
That's what I want to write about.

757
00:47:30,610 --> 00:47:32,030
What kind of dream is it?

758
00:47:32,490 --> 00:47:34,990
I'll share it with you once the scenario is done.

759
00:47:35,490 --> 00:47:36,200
Okay.

760
00:47:37,540 --> 00:47:42,920
You know, I also have a dream that I've been having since I was little.

761
00:47:43,920 --> 00:47:44,750
How does it go?

762
00:47:45,250 --> 00:47:47,960
Mine's a nightmare.

763
00:47:48,590 --> 00:47:50,880
I always wake up in a cold sweat.

764
00:47:50,880 --> 00:47:51,970
I don't even want to talk about it.

765
00:48:17,040 --> 00:48:17,990
Furukawa.

766
00:48:19,450 --> 00:48:20,370
Thank you.

767
00:48:20,910 --> 00:48:24,380
Today was the first time in a while I ate a meal with so many people.

768
00:48:24,380 --> 00:48:25,670
It was really fun.

769
00:48:26,130 --> 00:48:29,010
I was very warm, and it made me happy.

770
00:48:34,550 --> 00:48:37,560
I'm glad. I'm happy, too.

771
00:48:48,280 --> 00:48:53,950
Soon after that day, I saw the dream starting from where I'd left off last time.

772
00:49:00,540 --> 00:49:07,920
But this time, the dream didn't end with the repetition of hopeless situations.

773
00:49:09,800 --> 00:49:13,720
It had a turn where I could almost catch a glimmer of hope.

774
00:49:19,640 --> 00:49:22,730
Words echoed in my head.

775
00:49:25,190 --> 00:49:26,350
"The Tree of Promise."

776
00:49:27,610 --> 00:49:32,030
"At the end of this wilderness, there is the Tree of Promise."

777
00:49:32,900 --> 00:49:34,240
"It awaits you."

778
00:49:35,990 --> 00:49:37,240
Tree of Promise?

779
00:49:37,660 --> 00:49:38,910
Waiting for me?

780
00:49:39,490 --> 00:49:40,290
What is?

781
00:49:40,790 --> 00:49:41,490
Who is?

782
00:49:45,710 --> 00:49:48,540
It was clear to me what was waiting.

783
00:49:49,630 --> 00:49:54,880
It must the "someone" that I'd been searching for.

784
00:49:59,180 --> 00:50:01,930
Something burned inside of me.

785
00:50:02,140 --> 00:50:04,730
Something sparked inside my heart.

786
00:50:05,940 --> 00:50:08,810
I ran with everything I had.

787
00:50:09,940 --> 00:50:11,190
Aiming for the end of the wilderness...

788
00:50:12,030 --> 00:50:13,780
Aiming for the end of the life...

789
00:50:20,200 --> 00:50:22,160
Hey, Okazaki.

790
00:50:24,290 --> 00:50:25,250
Up here.

791
00:50:26,710 --> 00:50:27,620
Sunohara.

792
00:50:30,340 --> 00:50:33,300
He's my senpai, Yoshino. Yoshino Yusuke-san.

793
00:50:33,670 --> 00:50:35,880
This is Okazaki. Former basketball player.

794
00:50:36,220 --> 00:50:37,840
Currently a Theater Club member.

795
00:50:37,840 --> 00:50:39,010
Quit it.

796
00:50:41,850 --> 00:50:45,480
We're short on people. Do you want a part-time job, too?

797
00:50:45,480 --> 00:50:46,520
Y-Yeah...

798
00:50:46,890 --> 00:50:48,400
Give it some thought, Okazaki.

799
00:50:48,400 --> 00:50:49,900
The pay is pretty good.

800
00:50:49,900 --> 00:50:51,190
We're going to the next site.

801
00:50:51,610 --> 00:50:52,520
Coming.

802
00:50:53,610 --> 00:50:55,690
What time are you getting out, Sunohara?

803
00:51:07,830 --> 00:51:12,840
Yoshino-san used to be a famous musician in Tokyo.

804
00:51:13,460 --> 00:51:14,590
Musician?

805
00:51:16,460 --> 00:51:20,050
He was in a rock band and released a lot of CDs.

806
00:51:22,470 --> 00:51:24,350
But for some reason, he dropped out.

807
00:51:24,680 --> 00:51:27,850
Right now, he's come back to this city and is working like any other person.

808
00:51:31,100 --> 00:51:35,110
Doesn't that sound like how we
gave up on soccer and basketball?

809
00:51:35,480 --> 00:51:37,360
No, it's completely different.

810
00:51:37,360 --> 00:51:39,700
He went all the way to standing under the spotlight once.

811
00:51:41,280 --> 00:51:42,120
You're right.

812
00:51:49,620 --> 00:51:54,500
Nagisa. Okazaki What's-His-Name won't be coming tonight?

813
00:51:56,420 --> 00:51:57,880
Pardon me.

814
00:51:58,880 --> 00:52:00,380
I'm sorry.

815
00:52:01,510 --> 00:52:04,890
I can't make it to the Founders Festival's preparations at all.

816
00:52:05,560 --> 00:52:08,980
I'm in charge of Sound and you're Lighting.

817
00:52:10,480 --> 00:52:11,520
I see.

818
00:52:13,560 --> 00:52:15,900
Ibuki-sensei made the decision today.

819
00:52:16,480 --> 00:52:17,190
I see.

820
00:52:17,570 --> 00:52:20,650
But Furukawa's scenario is behind schedule.

821
00:52:23,070 --> 00:52:26,830
She might have to wing it on stage that day.

822
00:52:29,250 --> 00:52:33,290
Furukawa has it rough, but we might need to be ready for this thing, too.

823
00:52:34,960 --> 00:52:36,210
Go and see what happens.

824
00:52:36,540 --> 00:52:38,630
That's more fitting for us.

825
00:52:38,960 --> 00:52:40,670
Less things to worry about, right?

826
00:52:41,260 --> 00:52:43,180
Are you serious about this?

827
00:52:52,940 --> 00:52:56,360
The day of the Founders Festival came.

828
00:53:09,120 --> 00:53:11,540
What? You can't do that to us.

829
00:53:11,540 --> 00:53:13,540
Why are you teaching math in English class?

830
00:53:13,920 --> 00:53:17,500
Ah god. This is what I always get from silly students.

831
00:53:17,920 --> 00:53:21,210
Listen. Mathank you very much.

832
00:53:23,760 --> 00:53:25,760
Thank you for you time.

833
00:53:38,270 --> 00:53:40,110
You're joking, right, Furukawa?

834
00:53:41,440 --> 00:53:43,780
I'm sorry, can you repeat that?

835
00:53:45,070 --> 00:53:46,240
Furukawa-san?

836
00:53:47,410 --> 00:53:48,740
I'm sorry...

837
00:53:49,490 --> 00:53:54,410
I couldn't get the scenario done in time.

838
00:54:16,100 --> 00:54:17,730
This is so like us.

839
00:54:18,350 --> 00:54:24,650
The first New Theater Club's performance gets canceled.

840
00:54:30,530 --> 00:54:31,280
Um...

841
00:54:32,080 --> 00:54:34,830
I couldn't get the scenario done in time,

842
00:54:35,460 --> 00:54:39,040
but I plan on standing on the stage.

843
00:54:41,040 --> 00:54:42,340
Furukawa-san?

844
00:54:42,960 --> 00:54:47,590
It's complete inside me.

845
00:54:53,600 --> 00:54:58,810
B-But, Furukawa. We need to read the scenario at least once.

846
00:54:58,980 --> 00:55:00,810
Like for Lighting and Sound.

847
00:55:01,230 --> 00:55:03,730
Or else we won't have a clue what to do.

848
00:55:04,110 --> 00:55:06,240
No, it's fine.

849
00:55:06,570 --> 00:55:09,530
I'll give orders as I watch the stage.

850
00:55:10,200 --> 00:55:11,530
Sensei...

851
00:55:11,950 --> 00:55:16,250
Let's all trust the scenario Furukawa-san has in her heart.

852
00:55:18,750 --> 00:55:21,710
I'm sure it's a very wonderful story.

853
00:55:33,260 --> 00:55:35,270
Akio-san, over here.

854
00:55:38,020 --> 00:55:43,270
Let's see. Where is the auditorium Nagisa will be performing at?

855
00:55:44,150 --> 00:55:46,690
Looks like Nagisa won't be on stage until much later.

856
00:55:47,150 --> 00:55:49,240
Let's have lunch in the meantime.

857
00:55:49,860 --> 00:55:51,160
Yeah. That sounds good.

858
00:56:06,880 --> 00:56:07,760
I knew it.

859
00:56:08,260 --> 00:56:09,760
I knew I'd find you here.

860
00:56:13,050 --> 00:56:14,430
Have you had lunch?

861
00:56:15,970 --> 00:56:17,770
You won't be up until around evening.

862
00:56:17,770 --> 00:56:19,770
You won't last unless you eat something.

863
00:56:22,650 --> 00:56:27,030
We heard there's a cheap but good udon stand,
and Sunohara went dashing to it.

864
00:56:28,780 --> 00:56:32,700
I'm sorry. I don't think my stomach will accept it.

865
00:56:33,410 --> 00:56:34,660
Not much you can do about it, then.

866
00:56:35,240 --> 00:56:36,450
I'm sorry.

867
00:56:39,700 --> 00:56:43,750
I'm sorry for causing trouble for everyone.

868
00:56:44,420 --> 00:56:46,000
Stop apologizing!

869
00:56:46,540 --> 00:56:47,460
But...

870
00:56:47,750 --> 00:56:51,010
You will stand on the stage and do as you like.

871
00:56:51,470 --> 00:56:52,970
We'll follow you.

872
00:56:52,970 --> 00:56:54,140
That's what we decided on doing.

873
00:56:55,930 --> 00:56:58,390
Have confidence and do it with pride.

874
00:56:58,390 --> 00:57:03,140
Like Ibuki-sensei said, there's nothing more we can do than trust you.

875
00:57:04,350 --> 00:57:05,060
Yes!

876
00:57:05,360 --> 00:57:07,150
Yeah! That's what I want to hear.

877
00:57:07,150 --> 00:57:08,020
Yes!

878
00:57:08,780 --> 00:57:09,320
All right.

879
00:57:09,940 --> 00:57:10,940
Good.

880
00:57:13,490 --> 00:57:14,450
I'll see you later.

881
00:57:14,450 --> 00:57:17,370
Make sure you read over the scenario in your heart.

882
00:57:19,160 --> 00:57:19,990
What's wrong?

883
00:57:20,290 --> 00:57:23,460
I think I'm suddenly hungry.

884
00:57:23,960 --> 00:57:25,210
What?

885
00:57:25,750 --> 00:57:27,960
You're so unmanageable.

886
00:57:28,420 --> 00:57:29,590
Fine, wait here.

887
00:57:30,170 --> 00:57:31,510
I'll get you something.

888
00:57:42,390 --> 00:57:48,150
Let me share the reason why I want to do theater so much.

889
00:57:50,480 --> 00:57:56,950
My dad and mom used to work together as actors in a theatrical group.

890
00:57:57,620 --> 00:58:02,910
But after getting married and having me, they gave up on staying actors.

891
00:58:03,500 --> 00:58:08,880
I was physically weak when I was a child, so they chose to be with me all the time.

892
00:58:12,300 --> 00:58:17,300
That's why they quit the theater group,
moved to this city, and started a bakery.

893
00:58:17,840 --> 00:58:22,100
They figured a homemade bakery would let the family always be together.

894
00:58:25,020 --> 00:58:32,230
So... So standing on the stage is a way of thanking my parents.

895
00:58:32,730 --> 00:58:35,280
Showing how well I am...

896
00:58:35,780 --> 00:58:40,780
That I still remember what their dreams were.

897
00:58:48,960 --> 00:58:50,540
Something like that happens in this world, eh?

898
00:58:51,340 --> 00:58:55,720
To pick family over your own dreams...

899
00:58:56,130 --> 00:58:58,550
So you can find something like this if you look for it.

900
00:59:01,010 --> 00:59:04,520
It sounds like a story totally unrelated to me.

901
00:59:20,780 --> 00:59:22,330
What the hell are you saying?

902
00:59:22,330 --> 00:59:25,790
When you get that attitude,
you're supposed to slap them around.

903
00:59:25,790 --> 00:59:27,120
Like this?

904
00:59:27,910 --> 00:59:28,960
Where's my glasses?

905
00:59:34,340 --> 00:59:36,510
Did you bring a costume?

906
00:59:36,710 --> 00:59:39,470
Yes. I borrowed it from my mother.

907
00:59:40,130 --> 00:59:42,430
Let's go. It's almost time.

908
00:59:42,850 --> 00:59:43,510
Yes.

909
01:00:00,320 --> 01:00:00,990
Yo.

910
01:00:01,280 --> 01:00:02,700
Ah, Yoshino-senpai.

911
01:00:03,950 --> 01:00:06,990
I didn't know you were coming to the Founders Festival.

912
01:00:09,370 --> 01:00:11,670
When you're done, I'll be waiting at the usual place.

913
01:00:12,580 --> 01:00:13,330
Okay.

914
01:00:16,630 --> 01:00:18,380
Well, good luck.

915
01:00:19,510 --> 01:00:20,550
Yup. Thank you.

916
01:00:25,680 --> 01:00:29,270
Sensei, you were dating Yoshino-senpai?

917
01:00:29,270 --> 01:00:31,350
I never knew that.

918
01:00:31,350 --> 01:00:32,520
You just dropped something.

919
01:00:34,940 --> 01:00:36,570
Where? Where?

920
01:00:36,570 --> 01:00:37,320
Where?!

921
01:00:42,200 --> 01:00:46,370
Next is a solo play by the Theater Club.

922
01:00:46,740 --> 01:00:48,830
The Empty World.

923
01:00:58,500 --> 01:01:00,010
Lighting, stand by.

924
01:01:01,420 --> 01:01:06,100
First, flow Furukawa-san with the spotlight.

925
01:01:07,050 --> 01:01:07,720
Gotcha.

926
01:01:08,680 --> 01:01:10,060
Sound, ready?

927
01:01:10,600 --> 01:01:11,270
Counting down, ten seconds...

928
01:01:13,520 --> 01:01:14,400
Five seconds...

929
01:01:15,650 --> 01:01:18,020
Slowly come in.

930
01:01:18,860 --> 01:01:19,480
Two...

931
01:01:20,070 --> 01:01:20,860
One...

932
01:01:21,280 --> 01:01:21,900
Go!

933
01:01:31,200 --> 01:01:32,660
Sanae... That's...

934
01:01:33,330 --> 01:01:36,790
Yes. It's the dress I wore at our wedding.

935
01:01:36,790 --> 01:01:38,130
I gave it to Nagisa.

936
01:01:38,590 --> 01:01:39,750
Gave it to her?

937
01:01:40,130 --> 01:01:44,050
Yes. Since I won't have the chance to wear it again.

938
01:01:46,140 --> 01:01:47,890
Well, that's true.

939
01:01:50,680 --> 01:01:52,350
The empty world...

940
01:01:52,850 --> 01:01:54,810
What's there is wind...

941
01:01:55,770 --> 01:01:57,230
...a small ray of light...

942
01:01:57,730 --> 01:01:59,360
...occasional snow...

943
01:02:00,440 --> 01:02:05,740
...and me, who is so tired that there isn't even a tear to shed.

944
01:02:06,360 --> 01:02:08,240
Drop down the music a little.

945
01:02:08,820 --> 01:02:12,200
Sound of wind in the back. Louder slowly.

946
01:02:16,670 --> 01:02:19,000
How much time has passed?

947
01:02:20,000 --> 01:02:21,000
One month?

948
01:02:21,460 --> 01:02:22,670
Two months?

949
01:02:23,380 --> 01:02:26,880
Five years may have passed for all I know.

950
01:02:30,640 --> 01:02:36,310
These days, I can't even recall what I was waiting for.

951
01:02:37,350 --> 01:02:38,900
Change lighting to blue.

952
01:02:39,860 --> 01:02:40,980
Give it a soft feel to it.

953
01:02:42,070 --> 01:02:44,110
Yes, that's good.

954
01:02:47,700 --> 01:02:52,240
But the wind that comes from the ocean...

955
01:02:52,990 --> 01:02:55,710
The familiar, warm wind.

956
01:02:56,120 --> 01:03:00,710
Like the warmth of a mother's hand or a father's kindness.

957
01:03:01,670 --> 01:03:07,630
When that wind covers my body, I will regain my memory.

958
01:03:08,260 --> 01:03:11,680
I will become a little better and come alive once more.

959
01:03:12,100 --> 01:03:14,810
Overlap the sounds of wind and waves.

960
01:03:15,180 --> 01:03:17,270
Increase the volume of BGM a little over time.

961
01:03:17,270 --> 01:03:18,020
Roger.

962
01:03:19,020 --> 01:03:21,400
What I'm waiting for is...

963
01:03:21,980 --> 01:03:24,360
It's your voice.

964
01:03:25,110 --> 01:03:28,320
It's a very small, hesitant voice,

965
01:03:28,650 --> 01:03:33,740
but it's your beautiful voice
that represents your kind heart.

966
01:03:34,450 --> 01:03:38,620
Your voice soaks into my heart.

967
01:03:39,290 --> 01:03:41,830
Your voice and you...

968
01:03:42,210 --> 01:03:44,130
...are what I'm waiting for.

969
01:03:44,800 --> 01:03:46,840
Start Music 2.

970
01:03:47,170 --> 01:03:48,670
Slowly fade Music 1 out.

971
01:03:48,920 --> 01:03:51,180
Sunohara-kun, chase Furukawa-san.

972
01:04:07,490 --> 01:04:09,400
I run.

973
01:04:09,900 --> 01:04:13,160
I run for the end to the empty world.

974
01:04:22,420 --> 01:04:25,880
I heard a voice inside my heart.

975
01:04:27,250 --> 01:04:29,800
"Go to the end of the empty world."

976
01:04:30,090 --> 01:04:32,840
"Someone awaits you there."

977
01:04:33,470 --> 01:04:37,640
"For many, many years, that someone has been waiting for you."

978
01:04:38,600 --> 01:04:41,770
"Just as you were waiting."

979
01:04:47,320 --> 01:04:50,900
And in the end, this is what the voice said.

980
01:04:52,320 --> 01:04:54,820
Okazaki-kun. Continue the music.

981
01:04:55,830 --> 01:04:56,780
Okazaki-kun!

982
01:04:57,330 --> 01:05:01,750
"When you reach the end of the world, you shall witness..."

983
01:05:02,250 --> 01:05:06,960
"...the figure filled with life and shimmering gloriously!"

984
01:05:08,920 --> 01:05:11,510
"That is the Tree of Promise."

985
01:05:12,220 --> 01:05:13,340
This can't be!

986
01:05:14,510 --> 01:05:15,390
Okazaki-kun.

987
01:05:16,640 --> 01:05:20,350
"Someone is waiting for you under that tree!"

988
01:05:28,520 --> 01:05:33,400
Your solo play continued.

989
01:05:35,870 --> 01:05:39,700
There were many things in the way,
but you made it to the Tree of Promise.

990
01:05:40,870 --> 01:05:46,250
But I couldn't get any of the rest of the story into my head.

991
01:05:47,920 --> 01:05:57,680
I was shocked by the fact that for the longest time, you and I had been having the same dream, and I panicked.

992
01:05:58,890 --> 01:06:08,060
I panicked because I always thought I was the only one who dreamed of anything as lonely as this empty world.

993
01:06:09,940 --> 01:06:13,490
Furukawa... I never knew you shared the dream.

994
01:06:13,820 --> 01:06:18,450
You always smiled so kindly
and always acted so cheerfully.

995
01:06:19,280 --> 01:06:22,410
You would just laugh when you were in trouble, and yet you were...

996
01:06:31,170 --> 01:06:32,340
So dear to me.

997
01:06:33,880 --> 01:06:35,720
you are so dear to me.

998
01:06:36,720 --> 01:06:39,930
That's what I felt from the bottom of my heart.

999
01:06:49,900 --> 01:06:51,020
Tomoya-san.

1000
01:06:52,650 --> 01:06:53,400
Nagisa!

1001
01:06:53,980 --> 01:06:54,940
I love you!

1002
01:07:05,580 --> 01:07:08,790
After that, two springs went by.

1003
01:07:10,500 --> 01:07:12,590
It's because soon after the Founders Festival,

1004
01:07:12,590 --> 01:07:16,670
Nagisa's health went downhill and she had to be away from school for nearly a year.

1005
01:07:19,590 --> 01:07:26,520
In other words, Nagisa graduated from high school a year after us.

1006
01:07:26,980 --> 01:07:29,690
Nagisa, congratulations on your graduation!

1007
01:07:30,400 --> 01:07:37,990
After her graduation, when the sakura were in full bloom, we started living together...

1008
01:07:44,370 --> 01:07:45,580
...in this apartment.

1009
01:07:54,500 --> 01:07:55,250
Nagisa!

1010
01:07:59,050 --> 01:08:00,090
Good evening.

1011
01:08:00,090 --> 01:08:01,140
You're back late.

1012
01:08:02,010 --> 01:08:03,100
Sakagami.

1013
01:08:03,970 --> 01:08:07,770
I stopped by Furukawa Bread today,
and they asked me to bring this to you.

1014
01:08:11,150 --> 01:08:14,320
Sanae-san said she wanted you to eat these.

1015
01:08:16,440 --> 01:08:19,780
You aren't eating properly, are you?

1016
01:08:22,490 --> 01:08:26,700
I thought bread alone wouldn't be enough, so I'm thinking of making some soup.

1017
01:08:27,120 --> 01:08:28,450
Let me borrow your kitchen.

1018
01:08:31,830 --> 01:08:35,000
I heard you don't go to Furukawa Bread too often.

1019
01:08:36,670 --> 01:08:39,090
Ushio-chan's become pretty big.

1020
01:08:43,890 --> 01:08:44,800
Coming.

1021
01:08:46,810 --> 01:08:48,220
Hello.

1022
01:08:48,220 --> 01:08:49,850
What? Sunohara?!

1023
01:08:52,060 --> 01:08:55,110
Oh, Sakagami. You're here, too?

1024
01:08:55,110 --> 01:08:57,230
Wow, you're here from Tokyo?

1025
01:08:57,230 --> 01:08:58,440
Today's a weekday.

1026
01:08:58,440 --> 01:08:59,490
Do you have a day off?

1027
01:09:00,280 --> 01:09:03,070
Big companies have a thing called paid vacation.

1028
01:09:03,070 --> 01:09:07,200
Came on a bullet train and got on a local train. A long tiring trip.

1029
01:09:11,660 --> 01:09:13,420
Hey, former Theater Club.

1030
01:09:13,420 --> 01:09:14,710
Are you doing well?

1031
01:09:16,710 --> 01:09:20,670
If you were, I wouldn't have come.

1032
01:09:20,670 --> 01:09:21,510
But...

1033
01:09:26,010 --> 01:09:29,060
You're so hopeless; still depressed.

1034
01:09:29,060 --> 01:09:30,810
I heard you haven't been going to work at all.

1035
01:09:31,140 --> 01:09:33,890
Will you join us for dinner, Sunohara?
You haven't eaten yet, have you?

1036
01:09:34,310 --> 01:09:37,110
Yeah, I'll dig in. Thanks.

1037
01:09:37,690 --> 01:09:39,860
Okazaki, come over here.

1038
01:09:40,360 --> 01:09:41,690
Let's all eat together.

1039
01:09:44,950 --> 01:09:46,820
Let's go, Okazaki.

1040
01:09:46,820 --> 01:09:47,570
Come on.

1041
01:09:53,120 --> 01:09:56,790
Hey, wait a minute. Today's the 24th, isn't it?

1042
01:09:58,290 --> 01:10:01,760
It's the monthly anniversary of her death, so let me offer some incense.

1043
01:10:02,670 --> 01:10:04,010
Me, too.

1044
01:10:22,150 --> 01:10:23,400
It was fun.

1045
01:10:23,820 --> 01:10:25,700
Our life in the apartment.

1046
01:10:26,070 --> 01:10:29,370
It really was for a short time, but it was fun.

1047
01:10:31,830 --> 01:10:33,410
Have a good day.

1048
01:10:33,410 --> 01:10:34,200
Later.

1049
01:10:35,620 --> 01:10:42,630
I got employed full-time at the part-time position Yoshino-senpai first introduced me to after graduating.

1050
01:10:43,630 --> 01:10:45,300
Nagisa worked, too.

1051
01:10:45,590 --> 01:10:48,340
Four days a week at a nearby family restaurant.

1052
01:10:48,720 --> 01:10:50,930
Can I have some water?

1053
01:10:51,180 --> 01:10:53,930
Sir, this is your fifth cup.

1054
01:10:53,930 --> 01:10:56,560
It's fine, since I love water.

1055
01:10:56,980 --> 01:10:58,650
Watch me.

1056
01:11:05,900 --> 01:11:10,530
I often went to the shop with Sunohara, who hadn't left for Tokyo yet, and caused a lot of trouble for you.

1057
01:11:12,080 --> 01:11:14,910
We were actually visiting to see you.

1058
01:11:16,040 --> 01:11:19,040
To see you working hard with a smile.

1059
01:11:19,750 --> 01:11:21,880
We wanted to see you shine.

1060
01:11:22,290 --> 01:11:25,800
Hello. Welcome to Earnest Host.

1061
01:11:26,840 --> 01:11:34,220
Also, that small apartment really became like a house for the Big Dango Family.

1062
01:11:34,430 --> 01:11:37,180
Everyone would come visit us.

1063
01:11:37,600 --> 01:11:38,940
Akio's here!

1064
01:11:38,940 --> 01:11:40,150
Sanae's here!

1065
01:11:40,690 --> 01:11:43,480
The two of us make Akio-Sanae.

1066
01:11:43,940 --> 01:11:47,570
Sensei, why are you teaching math in English class?

1067
01:11:47,860 --> 01:11:52,070
Oh dear... Silly bakers always ask me that.

1068
01:11:52,070 --> 01:11:54,030
Listen this is the real,

1069
01:11:54,740 --> 01:11:57,000
mathank you very much.

1070
01:11:59,000 --> 01:12:00,710
You stole that joke!

1071
01:12:01,210 --> 01:12:02,880
Hello, Sunohara's here!

1072
01:12:03,290 --> 01:12:04,840
Sakagami Tomoyo's here!

1073
01:12:04,840 --> 01:12:06,380
Fujibayashi Kyou's here!

1074
01:12:06,760 --> 01:12:10,380
Three of us make the Suno-Saka-Kyou Trio!

1075
01:12:10,880 --> 01:12:12,300
Our apartment isn't a comedy house!

1076
01:12:12,300 --> 01:12:13,470
Enough of this!

1077
01:12:16,850 --> 01:12:18,770
Wow, looks like everyone's having fun here.

1078
01:12:19,520 --> 01:12:21,440
What's today's gathering about?

1079
01:12:22,440 --> 01:12:24,190
Yoshino-senpai! Ibuki-sensei!

1080
01:12:25,150 --> 01:12:28,150
We have the lovey-dovey couple!

1081
01:12:28,490 --> 01:12:31,490
I'm asking you what this gathering is about!

1082
01:12:31,490 --> 01:12:33,990
Nothing. We're just hanging out.

1083
01:12:34,490 --> 01:12:35,870
Is that so?

1084
01:12:36,120 --> 01:12:36,790
That's right.

1085
01:12:37,870 --> 01:12:41,420
All right then! Everyone, let's go!

1086
01:12:48,210 --> 01:12:52,340
Dango, dango, dango, dango.

1087
01:12:52,340 --> 01:12:56,350
Dango family is a big family.

1088
01:12:56,350 --> 01:13:02,600
Always a happy big family.

1089
01:13:02,890 --> 01:13:06,570
The house is always like a sports day.

1090
01:13:06,980 --> 01:13:11,070
Ready go, run run run. Family marathon.

1091
01:13:07,190 --> 01:13:09,530
I knew it wasn't me.

1092
01:13:10,030 --> 01:13:12,240
Everyone gathered around you.

1093
01:13:11,070 --> 01:13:14,660
Time for a bath. Get inside. Breath-holding competition.

1094
01:13:13,070 --> 01:13:14,360
Your kindness.

1095
01:13:14,660 --> 01:13:19,790
Dango. Dango's a big family.

1096
01:13:14,660 --> 01:13:15,740
Your cheerfulness.

1097
01:13:16,330 --> 01:13:22,120
Something about you that calmed everyone...
recreated the Big Dango Family here.

1098
01:13:24,670 --> 01:13:28,050
But... But who thought you'd...

1099
01:13:31,050 --> 01:13:32,420
See ya, Okazaki.

1100
01:13:33,050 --> 01:13:34,800
I'll go home today.

1101
01:13:34,800 --> 01:13:37,930
Do you like pasta? I'll make some next time I come.

1102
01:13:37,930 --> 01:13:39,510
She means spaghetti.

1103
01:13:45,060 --> 01:13:46,060
Bye.

1104
01:13:46,060 --> 01:13:47,730
Good night.

1105
01:13:54,740 --> 01:13:57,490
What's gone wrong with Okazaki?

1106
01:13:58,080 --> 01:14:00,290
He didn't say a single word to me in the end.

1107
01:14:00,790 --> 01:14:01,910
Sunohara.

1108
01:14:06,420 --> 01:14:07,710
There's nothing you can do.

1109
01:14:08,000 --> 01:14:09,500
We have to let time take care of it.

1110
01:14:10,090 --> 01:14:13,470
I'm so pathetic to be unable to do anything.

1111
01:14:32,150 --> 01:14:36,450
The baby seems to have
a healthy heart. It's developing well.

1112
01:14:36,820 --> 01:14:39,160
The problem lies with the mother.

1113
01:14:39,570 --> 01:14:43,290
Mother? So you mean with Nagisa?

1114
01:14:43,790 --> 01:14:46,920
She's been in and out of the hospital since she was young.

1115
01:14:47,710 --> 01:14:52,050
Her body is weaker than you think.

1116
01:14:52,420 --> 01:14:59,800
If she goes through labor and delivers the baby, the chances of her survival are very slim.

1117
01:14:59,800 --> 01:15:02,390
Isn't there a way to save both of them?

1118
01:15:02,640 --> 01:15:05,270
Please talk to your daughter.

1119
01:15:05,270 --> 01:15:07,600
We'll do the best we can based on her answer.

1120
01:15:10,810 --> 01:15:14,780
We have to tell Nagisa everything.

1121
01:15:15,400 --> 01:15:17,610
You think so, too, right, Tomoya-san?

1122
01:15:18,780 --> 01:15:19,530
Yes.

1123
01:15:27,210 --> 01:15:31,380
I already named the baby.

1124
01:15:32,540 --> 01:15:33,840
Nagisa...

1125
01:15:34,380 --> 01:15:36,840
It's Ushio.

1126
01:15:37,090 --> 01:15:40,970
Be it a boy or girl, it'll be Ushio.

1127
01:15:41,550 --> 01:15:43,930
Isn't it nice?

1128
01:15:44,720 --> 01:15:45,890
Nagisa...

1129
01:15:45,890 --> 01:15:47,600
I'm Nagisa.

1130
01:15:47,600 --> 01:15:50,350
But Ushio exists closer to the center of the ocean.

1131
01:15:50,980 --> 01:15:55,820
It's very noble and moves gallantly through the ocean.

1132
01:15:56,070 --> 01:16:02,530
I'm sure the baby won't be physically weak like me, and its heart will be much bigger and stronger.

1133
01:16:03,410 --> 01:16:04,490
Nagisa...

1134
01:16:04,910 --> 01:16:10,330
Right now, I'm thinking nothing else other than delivering this baby.

1135
01:16:10,710 --> 01:16:11,460
It'll be fine.

1136
01:16:12,130 --> 01:16:15,670
I want to meet this baby badly.

1137
01:16:15,670 --> 01:16:17,840
So I'm sure I'll be fine, too.

1138
01:16:18,340 --> 01:16:20,130
I have to be.

1139
01:16:28,480 --> 01:16:29,430
Nagisa...

1140
01:16:36,190 --> 01:16:38,030
Ushio-chan's born.

1141
01:16:38,570 --> 01:16:39,610
It's a girl.

1142
01:16:40,610 --> 01:16:41,530
How's the mother?

1143
01:16:41,910 --> 01:16:42,700
How's Nagisa doing?

1144
01:16:44,120 --> 01:16:48,040
The doctor said for the family to come immediately.

1145
01:16:48,790 --> 01:16:50,210
Ushio...

1146
01:16:51,460 --> 01:16:53,830
Look at Ushio, Tomoya-san.

1147
01:16:55,250 --> 01:16:55,920
Yeah.

1148
01:16:56,750 --> 01:17:00,340
I'm glad I met Ushio.

1149
01:17:01,220 --> 01:17:03,840
I'm really happy...

1150
01:17:04,890 --> 01:17:05,510
Yeah.

1151
01:17:06,220 --> 01:17:08,010
I'm happy for you, too, Nagisa.

1152
01:17:10,680 --> 01:17:20,280
That's right... I met you... under... many sakura...

1153
01:17:21,490 --> 01:17:22,570
Nagisa.

1154
01:17:23,450 --> 01:17:28,990
And then, we walked up the hill together.

1155
01:17:36,960 --> 01:17:43,170
At the top of the hill is Dad holding Ushio.

1156
01:17:44,260 --> 01:17:47,640
Mom's smiling...

1157
01:17:47,640 --> 01:17:49,720
Nagisa! Nagisa!

1158
01:17:49,720 --> 01:17:52,600
...and everyone's there.

1159
01:17:53,350 --> 01:17:54,730
Don't go Nagisa!

1160
01:17:55,400 --> 01:17:56,610
I'm so happy...

1161
01:17:56,980 --> 01:17:59,440
Everyone's waiting for me.

1162
01:18:00,980 --> 01:18:03,030
Nagisa! Don't go!

1163
01:18:03,030 --> 01:18:04,950
You don't have to walk up any hill!

1164
01:18:05,360 --> 01:18:07,280
You don't have to force yourself up!

1165
01:18:20,170 --> 01:18:21,920
Nagisa! Don't go!

1166
01:18:22,300 --> 01:18:24,720
Stay! Stay with me!

1167
01:18:29,970 --> 01:18:32,890
My beloved Tomoya-san...

1168
01:18:34,810 --> 01:18:36,390
Thank you.

1169
01:18:45,150 --> 01:18:45,820
Nagisa?

1170
01:18:48,530 --> 01:18:49,450
Nagisa?

1171
01:18:51,950 --> 01:18:53,950
Nagisa!!!

1172
01:19:13,350 --> 01:19:16,850
Soon after Nagisa died, I noticed something.

1173
01:19:20,230 --> 01:19:32,120
I noticed how I haven't had the nightmare I've been having since childhood for the longest time.

1174
01:19:36,080 --> 01:19:47,010
I think... after watching Nagisa's performance at the school's auditorium, I stopped having the nightmare.

1175
01:19:50,180 --> 01:19:55,600
But instead, ever since Nagisa died,
a new nightmare started.

1176
01:19:55,890 --> 01:20:02,650
To be precise, not a dream, but my life without Nagisa.

1177
01:20:03,400 --> 01:20:12,370
This everyday life that I face as reality became like the empty world in the nightmare.

1178
01:20:14,580 --> 01:20:17,500
If it's a dream, I can wake up from it as morning comes.

1179
01:20:18,000 --> 01:20:24,290
But there is no morning to this empty world.

1180
01:20:26,960 --> 01:20:33,260
The world where Nagisa doesn't exist will continue endlessly.

1181
01:20:45,270 --> 01:20:47,900
What? What time do you think it is?

1182
01:20:48,820 --> 01:20:53,240
I'm off to the night shift, but I had to talk to you.

1183
01:20:54,530 --> 01:20:56,200
There's nothing to talk about.

1184
01:20:59,410 --> 01:21:00,460
Go home.

1185
01:21:01,500 --> 01:21:03,210
Let me make some coffee.

1186
01:21:09,550 --> 01:21:10,800
So what do you want?

1187
01:21:11,420 --> 01:21:16,810
I heard you're leaving Ushio-chan with
her grandparents and you don't go see her at all.

1188
01:21:19,100 --> 01:21:20,890
I heard you haven't done much at all these past five years.

1189
01:21:21,810 --> 01:21:23,650
Not a good thing.

1190
01:21:25,730 --> 01:21:28,530
Yes, you're being just like me!

1191
01:21:30,740 --> 01:21:34,950
Just like how I wronged you after your mother died!

1192
01:21:37,370 --> 01:21:41,160
When your mother died, everything went black to me.

1193
01:21:41,160 --> 01:21:47,630
As a result, I made you feel lonely at the most crucial time in your life.

1194
01:21:48,420 --> 01:21:52,630
I couldn't pay attention to you at all,
and all I could do was bemoan my tragic life.

1195
01:21:53,420 --> 01:21:58,260
By the time I noticed it, you had already gone far away.

1196
01:21:59,470 --> 01:22:01,350
Just stay far way.

1197
01:22:01,810 --> 01:22:04,560
Don't come close to me, just like we haven't been.

1198
01:22:06,480 --> 01:22:08,520
I beg you. Please forgive me!

1199
01:22:09,150 --> 01:22:10,230
Quit it!

1200
01:22:10,570 --> 01:22:12,990
What kind of father kneels before his son?!

1201
01:22:13,700 --> 01:22:17,950
I didn't want to see you like that, so that's why I... I...

1202
01:22:24,080 --> 01:22:25,080
Leave me alone.

1203
01:22:25,460 --> 01:22:26,170
Go home.

1204
01:22:27,630 --> 01:22:29,540
I've made you angry again.

1205
01:22:30,840 --> 01:22:32,510
I'll be going now.

1206
01:22:35,380 --> 01:22:36,720
Oh yeah, Tomoya-kun.

1207
01:22:37,720 --> 01:22:38,680
What?

1208
01:22:39,220 --> 01:22:44,640
Ah, well... The rain will continue for a while, so don't catch a cold.

1209
01:22:45,730 --> 01:22:47,190
Mind your own business.

1210
01:22:48,310 --> 01:22:49,400
You're right.

1211
01:23:00,030 --> 01:23:03,120
Don't give me this crap...

1212
01:23:05,410 --> 01:23:07,040
Stop acting like my father...

1213
01:23:16,050 --> 01:23:17,050
Don't give me this...

1214
01:23:17,760 --> 01:23:19,050
Cut the crap!

1215
01:23:31,270 --> 01:23:33,070
Okazaki! Are you home?!

1216
01:23:35,190 --> 01:23:36,690
Get up!

1217
01:23:37,240 --> 01:23:38,740
The rain's gone already.

1218
01:23:39,410 --> 01:23:40,530
What are you doing?

1219
01:23:40,990 --> 01:23:42,280
Pack it up, Kouko.

1220
01:23:42,450 --> 01:23:43,370
Two shirts,

1221
01:23:43,830 --> 01:23:45,080
four boxers,

1222
01:23:45,080 --> 01:23:46,370
some socks,

1223
01:23:46,960 --> 01:23:48,670
and one change of long pants.

1224
01:23:48,870 --> 01:23:51,580
Okay. I'll pick and choose some other stuff.

1225
01:23:52,040 --> 01:23:53,210
Wash your face.

1226
01:23:53,210 --> 01:23:54,050
Brush your teeth.

1227
01:23:54,460 --> 01:23:55,670
Don't waste any time.

1228
01:23:56,760 --> 01:23:58,340
Wh-What is this about?

1229
01:23:58,760 --> 01:24:00,010
You're going on a trip.

1230
01:24:00,260 --> 01:24:01,720
I'll hear your complaints later.

1231
01:24:01,720 --> 01:24:02,470
Just do as I say.

1232
01:24:04,390 --> 01:24:05,560
Packed and ready!

1233
01:24:06,100 --> 01:24:07,930
All right then, off you go.

1234
01:24:10,190 --> 01:24:11,520
Hop in.

1235
01:24:16,070 --> 01:24:19,030
Trip you said? Where are we going?

1236
01:24:19,570 --> 01:24:20,700
Just a little somewhere.

1237
01:24:20,700 --> 01:24:21,820
Somewhere?

1238
01:24:22,200 --> 01:24:25,200
Shut up. Keep your mouth shut and sit.

1239
01:24:25,200 --> 01:24:25,950
That's right.

1240
01:24:29,750 --> 01:24:32,130
Hey! Hey!

1241
01:24:33,710 --> 01:24:35,170
All right, hop in.

1242
01:24:36,750 --> 01:24:37,760
Sunohara?

1243
01:24:40,880 --> 01:24:42,800
Sunohara, were you able to book the tickets?

1244
01:24:43,260 --> 01:24:44,220
Yes, Sir!

1245
01:24:44,220 --> 01:24:46,010
Got everyone's seats reserved.

1246
01:24:46,640 --> 01:24:47,720
Great!

1247
01:24:47,930 --> 01:24:49,850
What?

1248
01:24:50,440 --> 01:24:52,270
Reserved seats? Everyone?

1249
01:24:52,270 --> 01:24:53,150
What is this about?

1250
01:24:53,810 --> 01:24:55,940
Hey, over here.

1251
01:24:55,940 --> 01:24:56,900
Hello.

1252
01:24:58,860 --> 01:25:01,110
Come on, hop on in.

1253
01:25:01,110 --> 01:25:02,110
Okay.

1254
01:25:06,530 --> 01:25:07,700
There's your bento.

1255
01:25:08,290 --> 01:25:10,000
Here's yours Sunohara.

1256
01:25:10,000 --> 01:25:10,660
Woohoo.

1257
01:25:11,290 --> 01:25:14,420
We woke up early and made them together.

1258
01:25:15,290 --> 01:25:16,420
This looks amazing.

1259
01:25:16,420 --> 01:25:17,460
Good work.

1260
01:25:18,000 --> 01:25:19,880
Eat up, Okazaki.

1261
01:25:19,880 --> 01:25:21,050
You haven't had breakfast, right?

1262
01:25:21,920 --> 01:25:23,720
What is this about?!

1263
01:25:26,350 --> 01:25:28,930
I don't understand, but you're all being too weird!

1264
01:25:32,270 --> 01:25:34,100
Senpai! What is this about?!

1265
01:25:34,730 --> 01:25:35,810
A camp trip.

1266
01:25:36,860 --> 01:25:37,820
Camp?

1267
01:25:38,270 --> 01:25:41,320
That's right. It's the Big Dango Family camp trip.

1268
01:25:41,320 --> 01:25:44,410
We reserved a lodge by a beach for a week.

1269
01:25:44,410 --> 01:25:45,660
We're all going to have a camp there.

1270
01:25:46,570 --> 01:25:47,990
Big Dango Family...

1271
01:25:47,990 --> 01:25:49,160
Camp trip...

1272
01:25:49,580 --> 01:25:52,040
I can't go along with this.

1273
01:25:52,750 --> 01:25:55,290
She's not with us anymore...

1274
01:25:56,250 --> 01:25:57,630
Nagisa's gone!

1275
01:26:06,430 --> 01:26:07,140
I'll go home.

1276
01:26:07,680 --> 01:26:09,560
I'll get off at the next station.

1277
01:26:10,600 --> 01:26:11,970
I won't let you.

1278
01:26:12,640 --> 01:26:14,890
We're taking you no matter what.

1279
01:26:18,440 --> 01:26:22,030
I was asked to about ten days ago by a certain person.

1280
01:26:22,360 --> 01:26:25,200
So I will take you.

1281
01:26:26,240 --> 01:26:26,910
By who?

1282
01:26:27,410 --> 01:26:28,950
I can't tell you that.

1283
01:26:32,750 --> 01:26:34,750
Please. And I'm sorry.

1284
01:26:35,540 --> 01:26:38,130
Tomoya can't stand on his own yet.

1285
01:26:38,500 --> 01:26:42,210
Please save him with all of your support.

1286
01:26:43,090 --> 01:26:44,090
Father...

1287
01:26:45,260 --> 01:26:49,850
He booked the lodge and put together today's plan.

1288
01:26:50,810 --> 01:26:51,640
Who?!

1289
01:26:52,220 --> 01:26:54,100
You'll figure it out one day.

1290
01:26:54,100 --> 01:26:56,350
Once you can stand on your own, you will.

1291
01:27:20,750 --> 01:27:24,460
Let's see. We're supposed to get picked up at the platform.

1292
01:27:25,090 --> 01:27:27,680
Hey, Sunohara. Go check the fifth platform.

1293
01:27:27,680 --> 01:27:28,430
Okay.

1294
01:27:28,890 --> 01:27:31,350
Sakagami and Fujibayashi, go check the ticket counter.

1295
01:27:31,350 --> 01:27:32,180
Okay.

1296
01:27:32,680 --> 01:27:35,140
Okazaki, you go check the second platform.

1297
01:27:40,810 --> 01:27:41,690
Second...

1298
01:27:42,480 --> 01:27:43,520
Second platform...

1299
01:27:45,230 --> 01:27:47,070
Did Okazaki go?

1300
01:27:47,360 --> 01:27:50,160
Yeah. He just went on his way.

1301
01:28:47,300 --> 01:28:49,300
This is Dango.

1302
01:28:49,300 --> 01:28:50,680
I'll give it to you.

1303
01:28:56,180 --> 01:28:56,930
Watch out!

1304
01:29:12,780 --> 01:29:13,780
Papa.

1305
01:29:15,120 --> 01:29:17,660
Yeah. Hello, Ushio.

1306
01:29:18,410 --> 01:29:19,830
Hello.

1307
01:29:20,330 --> 01:29:20,960
Yeah.

1308
01:29:29,800 --> 01:29:37,050
It was only for a moment, but I saw
the dream again from where I'd left off.

1309
01:29:38,720 --> 01:29:43,190
Under the Tree of Promise, was you, Nagisa.

1310
01:29:43,940 --> 01:29:45,190
You stood there.

1311
01:29:46,310 --> 01:29:47,480
With a smile...

1312
01:29:48,110 --> 01:29:51,320
With your usual lovely smile.

1313
01:29:53,320 --> 01:29:55,320


1314
01:30:34,320 --> 01:30:51,170
Tookude tookude yureteru inaho no umi

1315
01:30:34,320 --> 01:30:51,170
Far away, far away, the sea of rice plants wavers

1316
01:30:53,550 --> 01:31:10,400
Ho wo age ho wo age mezashita omoi deto

1317
01:30:53,550 --> 01:31:10,400
Raising the rice, raising the rice, we aimed for the memory

1318
01:31:12,690 --> 01:31:21,530
Bokura wa kyou made no

1319
01:31:12,690 --> 01:31:21,530
Do we remember the sad things that have happened before today,

1320
01:31:21,740 --> 01:31:33,920
Kanashii koto zenbu oboeteruka, wasuretaka

1321
01:31:21,740 --> 01:31:33,920
or have we forgotten them?

1322
01:31:58,700 --> 01:32:10,500
Kuroi sono hitomi wa
Takusan no mirai utsusu

1323
01:31:58,700 --> 01:32:10,500
Your black pupils
Reflect the many futures

1324
